const QUESTIONS = [{"num": 1, "en": "Any voluntary religious headwear can be worn.", "fr": "Tout couvre -chef religieux volontaire peut être porté.", "es": "Se puede llevar cualquier tocado religioso volontario.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.5 / 2.1.2(b)"}, {"num": 2, "en": "The Karate Gi jacket must be more than three-quarters thigh length.", "fr": "La veste du Karate Gi doit descendre au - delà des trois quarts de la cuisse.", "es": "La chaqueta de Karate Gi debe tener una longitud superior a tres cuartos del muslo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(e)"}, {"num": 3, "en": "The Karate Gi trousers must cover at least two-thirds of the shin.", "fr": "Le pantalon de karaté doit recouvrir au moins les deux tiers du tibia.", "es": "Los pantalones de Karate Gi deben cubrir al menos dos tercios de la espinilla.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(j)"}, {"num": 4, "en": "The Karate Gi jacket sleeves must be no longer than the bend of the wrist.", "fr": "Les manches de la veste du Karate Gi ne doit pas dépasser le pli du poignet.", "es": "Le manga de la chaqueta de Karate Gi no debe ser más larga que el pliegue de la muñeca.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(h)"}, {"num": 5, "en": "If an Athlete's Karate Gi jacket sleeves are too long and a suitable replacement cannot be found in time the Referee can allow him to turn them up on the inside.", "fr": "Si les manches de la veste du Karate Gi d'un athlète sont trop longues et qu'un remplacement approprié ne peut pas être trouvé à temps, l'arbitre peut lui permettre de les retrousser à l'intérieur.", "es": "Si las mangas de la chaqueta de Karate Gi de un atleta son demasiado largas y no se puede encontrar un recambio adecuado a tiempo, el árbitro puede permitirle que se las suba por dentro.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(i)"}, {"num": 6, "en": "Athletes can wear 1 or 2 discreet rubber bands on a single ponytail. Ribbons, beads and other decorations are prohibited.", "fr": "Les athlètes peuvent porter 1 ou 2 élastiques discrets sur une seule queue de cheval. Les rubans, perles et autres décorations sont interdits.", "es": "Los atletas pueden llevar una o dos gomas discretas en una sola coleta. Diademas, cadenas y otros adornos están prohibidos.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.4"}, {"num": 7, "en": "Earrings are allowed if they are covered with tape.", "fr": "Les boucles d'oreilles sont autorisées si elles sont recouvertes de ruban adhésif.", "es": "Los pendientes están permitidos si están cubiertos con cinta adhesiva.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.6 / 2.1.2(c)"}, {"num": 8, "en": "Metallic teeth braces can be worn at the Athlete's own risk if approved by the Referee and the Official Doctor.", "fr": "Les appareils dentaires métalliques peuvent être portés aux risques et périls de l’athlète s'ils sont approuvés par l'arbitre et le médecin officiel.", "es": "Se pueden llevar aparatos dentales metálicos por cuenta y riesgo del atleta si lo aprueban el árbitro y el médico oficial.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.6"}, {"num": 9, "en": "Athletes must bow properly to each other at the start and end of the bout.", "fr": "Les athlètes doivent saluer correctement au début et à la fin du combat.", "es": "Los atletas deben saludarse correctamente al comienzo y al final del combate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.4"}, {"num": 10, "en": "The Coach can change the team fighting order during a match.", "fr": "L'entraîneur peut changer l'ordre de combat de l'équipe pendant un match.", "es": "El entrenador puede cambiar el orden de combate por equipos durante un encuentro.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.6.5 / 3.6.6 (locked once notified until the round is completed)"}, {"num": 11, "en": "If an Athlete is injured in an individual bout the Coach can enter a replacement if he notifies the Organising Commission first.", "fr": "Si un athlète est blessé lors d'un combat individuel, l'entraîneur peut inscrire un remplaçant s'il en avise d'abord la commission d'organisation.", "es": "Si un atleta se lesiona en un combate individual, el entrenador puede inscribir a un sustituto si lo notifica primero a la Comisión Organizadora.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.1 (no individual-bout replacement provision)"}, {"num": 12, "en": "Each Judge must be equipped with a red and a blue flag or joysticks.", "fr": "Chaque juge doit être équipé d'un drapeau rouge et d'un drapeau bleu ou des joysticks.", "es": "Cada juez debe estar equipado con una bandera roja y una azul o joysticks.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 1.7"}, {"num": 13, "en": "If two teams have the same number of victories and points, a deciding bout will be held.", "fr": "Si deux équipes ont le même nombre de victoires et de points, un combat décisif aura lieu.", "es": "Si dos equipos tienen el mismo número de victorias y puntos, se celebrará un combate decisivo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.5.2"}, {"num": 14, "en": "The Match Supervisor (KANSA) will be equipped with only a whistle.", "fr": "L'arbitre de match (KANSA) ne sera équipé que d'un sifflet.", "es": "El Supervisor del encuentro (KANSA) estará equipado únicamente con un silbato.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 1.8"}, {"num": 15, "en": "Disqualification by KIKEN means that the Athletes are disqualified from that category.", "fr": "La disqualification par KIKEN signifie que les athlètes sont disqualifiés de cette catégorie.", "es": "La descalificación por KIKEN significa que los atletas quedan descalificados de esa categoría.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 6.4"}, {"num": 16, "en": "Heels of more than 4 cm must not be worn with the uniform.", "fr": "Il est interdit de porter des talons de plus de 4 cm avec l'uniforme.", "es": "No se podrán llevar tacones de más de 4 cm con el uniforme.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.1.2(e)"}, {"num": 17, "en": "Senior Male bouts are three minutes, and Senior Female, Cadets, and Juniors, two minutes.", "fr": "Les combats masculins seniors durent trois minutes, et les combats féminins seniors, cadets et juniors, deux minutes.", "es": "Los combates de Senior Masculino son de tres minutos, y los Senior Femeninos, Cadetes y Juniors, de dos minutos.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 5.1 (Senior Female = 3 min, not 2)"}, {"num": 18, "en": "Kumite team members can wear any type of Karate Gi.", "fr": "Les membres de l'équipe de Kumite peuvent porter n'importe quel type de Karate Gi.", "es": "Los miembros del equipo de Kumite pueden usar cualquier tipo de Karate Gi.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1"}, {"num": 19, "en": "Different Karate Gi brands can be used for team members.", "fr": "Différentes marques de Karate Gi peuvent être utilisées pour les membres de l'équipe.", "es": "Se pueden utilizar diferentes marcas de Karate Gi para los miembros del equipo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(a)"}, {"num": 20, "en": "An Athlete does not need to change the jacket if the ties are torn off during the bout.", "fr": "Un athlète n'a pas besoin de changer de veste si les ficelles sont déchirées pendant le combat.", "es": "Un atleta no necesita cambiar la chaqueta si los lazos se rompen durante el combate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(g)"}, {"num": 21, "en": "Athletes can wear any white Karate Gi.", "fr": "Les athlètes peuvent porter n'importe quel Karate Gi blanc.", "es": "Los atletas pueden usar cualquier Karate Gi blanco.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1"}, {"num": 22, "en": "A fast combination of CHUDAN KERI and TSUKI each of which score in their own right will be given IPPON.", "fr": "Une combinaison rapide de CHUDAN KERI et TSUKI dont chacun marque recevra IPPON.", "es": "Con una combinación rápida de CHUDAN KERI y TSUKI, cada uno de los cuales puntúa correctamente, se dará IPPON.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.3 / 8.6 (combo scores WAZA-ARI, not IPPON)"}, {"num": 23, "en": "In Senior bouts a light \"skin touch\" to the throat does not need to result in a warning or penalty provided there is no injury.", "fr": "Dans les combats seniors, un léger \"skin touch\" à la gorge ne doit pas entraîner d'avertissement ou de pénalité à condition qu'il n'y ait pas de blessure.", "es": "En los encuentros Senior, un ligero toque de guante \"skin touch\" en la garganta no tiene por qué dar lugar a una advertencia o penalización, siempre que no haya una lesión.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.8 / 10.4.6 (no contact allowed to throat, regardless of injury)"}, {"num": 24, "en": "A kick in the groin will not result in a penalty provided the offender did not do it intentionally.", "fr": "Un coup de pied dans l'aine n'entraînera pas de pénalité à condition que le fautif ne l'ait pas fait intentionnellement.", "es": "Una patada en la ingle no dará lugar a penalización siempre que el infractor no lo haya hecho intencionadamente.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.1(2) / 10.4.2"}, {"num": 25, "en": "For Athletes under 14 years of age, the WKF approved protective helmet is compulsory.", "fr": "Pour les athlètes âgés de moins de 14 ans, le port du casque de protection homologué par la WKF est obligatoire.", "es": "Para los atletas menores de 14 años, es obligatorio el uso del casco protector homologado por la WKF.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.7(g)"}, {"num": 26, "en": "If SENSHU is withdrawn when it is less than 15 seconds left of the bout, no further SENSHU can be awarded to either Athlete.", "fr": "Si SENSHU est retiré alors qu'il reste moins de 15 secondes avant la fin du combat, aucun autre SENSHU ne peut être accordé à l'un ou l'autre des athlètes.", "es": "Si se retira el SENSHU cuando quedan menos de 15 segundos de combate, no se podrá conceder más SENSHU a ninguno de los atletas.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.10"}, {"num": 27, "en": "If an Athlete, that has been awarded SENSHU, receives a warning for avoiding combat when there is less than 15 seconds left of the bout – the Athlete will automatically forfeit this advantage.", "fr": "Si un athlète qui a reçu SENSHU reçoit un avertissement pour éviter le combat alors qu'il reste moins de 15 secondes du combat, le athlète perdra automatiquement cet avantage.", "es": "Si un atleta al que se le ha concedido SENSHU recibe una advertencia por evitar el combate cuando quedan menos de 15 segundos de combate, el atleta perderá automáticamente esta ventaja.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.8 / 10.4.16"}, {"num": 28, "en": "Voluntary religious headwear must be approved by WKF.", "fr": "Les couvre -chefs religieux volontaires doivent être approuvés par la WKF.", "es": "Los tocados religiosos voluntarios deben ser aprobados por la WKF.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.5 / 2.1.2(b)"}, {"num": 29, "en": "The WKF Competition Supervisor, or the Organizing Commission, can allow Coaches to use any t -shirt instead of the track suit jacket.", "fr": "Le superviseur de la compétition de la WKF, ou la commission d'organisation, peut autoriser les entraîneurs à utiliser n'importe quel t-shirt à la place de l aveste de survêtement.", "es": "El Supervisor de Competición de la WKF o la Comisión Organizadora pueden permitir a los entrenadores usar cualquier camiseta en lugar de la chaqueta del chándal.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.3.3 (Chief Referee, not Competition Supervisor/OC; not any t-shirt)"}, {"num": 30, "en": "HANSOKU CHUI is given if the Athlete's potential for winning has been reduced by the opponent's foul.", "fr": "HANSOKU CHUI est donné si le potentiel de victoire d'athlète a été réduit par la faute de l'adversaire.", "es": "HANSOKU CHUI si el potencial del atleta para ganar ha sido reducido por la falta del oponente.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.2.1"}, {"num": 31, "en": "The weight tolerance admitted for male and female is 0.5 kg.", "fr": "La tolérance de poids admise pour les hommes et les femmes 0,5 kg.", "es": "La tolerancia de peso admitida para hombres y mujeres es de 0,5 kg.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.2.2(d) (male 0.2kg, female 0.5kg)"}, {"num": 32, "en": "HANSOKU is imposed for very serious rules infractions.", "fr": "HANSOKU est imposé pour des infractions très graves aux règles.", "es": "HANSOKU se impone por infracciones muy graves de las reglas.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.1"}, {"num": 33, "en": "SHIKKAKU can only be imposed after a warning has been given.", "fr": "SHIKKAKU ne peut être imposé qu'après un avertissement.", "es": "SHIKKAKU sólo puede imponerse después de que se haya dado una advertencia.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.1 / 10.4.17 (can be direct)"}, {"num": 34, "en": "If an Athlete acts maliciously, SHIKKAKU and not HANSOKU is the correct penalty.", "fr": "Si un athlète agit avec malveillance, SHIKKAKU est la sanction correcte et non HANSOKU", "es": "Si un atleta actúa maliciosamente, SHIKKAKU y no HANSOKU es la penalización correcta.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.1"}, {"num": 35, "en": "If an Athlete acts maliciously, HANSOKU is the correct penalty.", "fr": "Si un athlète agit de manière malveillante, HANSOKU est la sanction correcte.", "es": "Si un atleta actúa maliciosamente, HANSOKU es la penalización correcta.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.1"}, {"num": 36, "en": "An Athlete can be given SHIKKAKU if the behaviour of the Coach or non - combatant members of the Athlete's delegation is considered to harm the prestige and honour of Karate -Do.", "fr": "Un athlète peut recevoir SHIKKAKU si le comportement de l'entraîneur ou des membres non combattants de la délégation du athlète est considéré comme portant atteinte au prestige et à l'honneur du Karate -Do.", "es": "Se puede dar SHIKKAKU a un atleta si se considera que el comportamiento del entrenador o de los miembros no combatientes de la delegación del atleta daña el prestigio y el honor del Karate -Do.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.1 / 9.1.4 (Coach is banned, Athlete is not given SHIKKAKU for this)"}, {"num": 37, "en": "For individual competition, the Round - robin system followed by quarterfinals, semifinals and final is applied.", "fr": "Pour les compétitions individuelles, le système round -robin suivi des quarts de finale, des demi -finales et de la finale est appliqué.", "es": "Para la competición individual, se aplica el sistema round -robin seguido de cuartos de final, semifinales y final.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.4.1-3.4.3 (default is elimination w/ repechage, not always round-robin)"}, {"num": 38, "en": "There are five criteria to be met in determining a score.", "fr": "Cinq critères doivent être remplis pour déterminer un score", "es": "Hay cinco criterios que deben cumplirse para determinar una puntuación.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.5 (six criteria, not five)"}, {"num": 39, "en": "A male team must present a minimum of five Athletes for the initial round.", "fr": "Une équipe masculine doit présenter un minimum de cinq athlètes pour le premier tour.", "es": "Un equipo masculino debe presentar un mínimo de cinco atletas para la ronda inicial.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.5.1"}, {"num": 40, "en": "Male Kumite teams in the elimination format comprise five to seven members with five competing in the first round.", "fr": "Les équipes masculines en système d'élimination sont composées de cinq à sept membres, dont cinq s'affrontent dans le premier tour.", "es": "Los equipos masculinos en el formato de eliminatión se componen de cinco a siete miembros de los cuales cinco compiten en la primera ronda.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.5.1"}, {"num": 41, "en": "A female team must present a minimum of two Athletes for the initial round.", "fr": "Une équipe féminine doit présenter au minimum deux athlètes pour le premier tour.", "es": "Un equipo femenino debe presentar un mínimo de dos atletas para la ronda inicial.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.5.2 (initial match needs 3, not 2)"}, {"num": 42, "en": "If the Coach continues to interfere after the first warning, the Referee will stop the bout, approach again and ask the Coach to leave the Tatami.", "fr": "Si l'entraîneur continue d'interférer après le premier avertissement, l'arbitre arrêtera le combat, s'approchera à nouveau de l'entraîneur et lui demandera de quitter le tatami.", "es": "Si el entrenador continúa interfiriendo después de la primera advertencia, el árbitro detendrá el combate, se acercará de nuevo al entrenador y le pedirá que abandone el tatami.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.4 (two-step procedure carried over from pre-2026 rules; still a valid exercise of the Referee's discretionary authority)"}, {"num": 43, "en": "If AKA scores just as AO steps outside of the competition area, both the score and warning or penalty can be given.", "fr": "Si AKA marque juste au moment où AO sort de la zone de combat, le score et l'avertissement ou la pénalité peuvent être donnés.", "es": "Si AKA puntúa justo cuando AO sale del área de competición, se puede dar tanto el punto como la advertencia o penalización.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.3 (no JOGAI given to the scored-upon exiting athlete)"}, {"num": 44, "en": "If an Athlete has been physically propelled from the area, JOGAI will be given.", "fr": "Si un athlète a été physiquement propulsé hors de la zone, JOGAI sera donné.", "es": "Si un atleta ha sido impulsado físicamente fuera del área, se dará JOGAI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.13 (exception - no JOGAI)"}, {"num": 45, "en": "In Premier League competition, the losers to the finalists in the quarterfinals and semifinals compete for the bronze medals.", "fr": "En compétition de Premier League, les perdants des finalistes, des quarts de finale et des demi -finales se disputent les médailles de bronze.", "es": "En la competición de la Premier League, los perdedores ante los finalistas en cuartos de final y semifinales compiten por las medallas de bronce.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.7.1"}, {"num": 46, "en": "In Round -robin, in cases where there is a tie between two or more Athletes in a group, having the same number of total points, the first criterion to consider is the highest World Ranking at the date of the competition.", "fr": "Dans round -robin, en cas d'égalité entre deux athlètes ou plus d'un même groupe ayant le même nombre de points au total, le premier critère à prendre en compte est le meilleur classement mondial à la date de la compétition.", "es": "En round -robin, en caso de que haya un empate entre dos o más atletas de un grupo que tengan el mismo número de puntos totales, el primer criterio a considerar es la clasificación mundial más alta a fecha de la competición.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.3.1 (first criterion is head-to-head result, ranking is 8th)"}, {"num": 47, "en": "It is possible for an Athlete to be disqualified from a bout (HANSOKU) and continue the competition.", "fr": "Il est possible qu'un athlète soit disqualifié d'un combat (HANSOKU) et continue la compétition.", "es": "Es posible que un atleta sea descalificado de un combate (HANSOKU) y continúe la competición.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.3.2"}, {"num": 48, "en": "An Athlete who scores and exits the area before the Referee calls YAME will not receive JOGAI.", "fr": "Un athlète qui marque et quitte la zone avant que l'arbitre annonce YAME ne recevra pas JOGAI.", "es": "Un atleta que puntué y salga del área antes de que el árbitro diga YAME, no recibirá JOGAI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.2"}, {"num": 49, "en": "Athletes cannot be given penalties after the time-up bell has signalled the end of a bout.", "fr": "Les athlètes ne peuvent pas se voir infliger de pénalités après que la sonnerie du temps écoulé ait signalé la fin d'un combat.", "es": "Los atletas no pueden ser penalizados después de que la señal de tiempo haya señalado el final de un combate.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.17 (SHIKKAKU may be imposed after the bout)"}, {"num": 50, "en": "Any technique to the face, head or neck, which causes injury will be warned or penalised unless it is the recipient's own fault.", "fr": "Toute technique au visage, à la tête ou au cou qui cause une blessure sera avertie ou pénalisée à moins que ce ne soit la faute du receveur.", "es": "Cualquier técnica a la cara, cabeza o cuello que cause lesión será advertida o penalizada a menos que sea culpa del receptor.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.2 / 10.4.6"}, {"num": 51, "en": "In Cadet and Junior competition JODAN techniques are allowed to make \"skin touch\" provided there is no injury.", "fr": "Dans les compétitions Cadet et Junior, les techniques JODAN sont autorisés avec un \"skin touch\" à condition qu'il n'y ait pas de blessure.", "es": "En las competiciones Cadete y Junior, las técnicas de JODAN permiten «skin touch», siempre que no haya lesiones.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.9 (also 8.8)"}, {"num": 52, "en": "In Senior competition a light touch is allowed for JODAN punches, and a greater tolerance is allowed for JODAN kicks.", "fr": "En compétition senior, une touche légère est autorisée pour les coups de poing JODAN, et une plus grande tolérance est autorisée pour les coups de pied JODAN.", "es": "En la competición Senior, se permite un toque ligero para las técnicas de puño JODAN y una mayor tolerancia para las patadas JODAN.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.8"}, {"num": 53, "en": "An already qualified Athlete cannot be disqualified for misconduct (SHIKKAKU) at the end of the Round - robin.", "fr": "Un athlète déjà qualifié ne peut pas être disqualifié pour mauvaise conduite (SHIKKAKU) à la fin du round -robin.", "es": "Un atleta ya clasificado no puede ser descalificado por mala conducta (SHIKKAKU) al final del round -robin.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.3.3 (rule addresses this happening)"}, {"num": 54, "en": "If a variation of the competition format other than described in the rules is to be applied for a particular tournament, this has to be clearly announced in the tournament bulletin.", "fr": "Si une variation du format de compétition autre que celle décrite dans les règles doit être appliquée pour un tournoi particulier, cela doit être clairement annoncé dans le bulletin du tournoi.", "es": "Si se va a aplicar una variación del formato de competición distinta a la descrita en el reglamento para un torneo en particular, deberá anunciarse claramente en el boletín del torneo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.10"}, {"num": 55, "en": "If an Athlete has been asked before the bout starts, and confirms wearing a groin guard, and it later proves that this is not so, the Athlete will receive SHIKKAKU.", "fr": "Si, avant le début du combat, on demande à un athlète s'il porte un coquille et qu'il répond par l'affirmative, mais qu'il s'avère par la suite que ce n'est pas le cas, l'athlète se verra infliger un SHIKKAKU.", "es": "Si se le pregunta a un atleta antes de que comience el combate si lleva protector de ingle y este lo confirma, pero posteriormente se comprueba que no es así, se le impondrá una sanción de SHIKKAKU.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.14"}, {"num": 56, "en": "When the Judges see a score, they will immediately signal it with their joystick or flag.", "fr": "Lorsque les juges voient un score, ils le signalent immédiatement avec des joysticks ou des drapeaux.", "es": "Cuando los jueces vean una puntuación, señalarán inmediatamente con los joysticks o las banderas.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.4.1(1) / 1.7"}, {"num": 57, "en": "The Referee Panel is composed of one Tatami Manager and three Tatami Manager Assistants.", "fr": "Le panel d'arbitres est composé d'un tatami manager et trois tatami manager assistants.", "es": "El panel arbitral está compuesto por un tatami manager y tres asistentes del tatami manager.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 4.1.1 vs 4.3.1 (that's Supporting Officials, not the Referee Panel)"}, {"num": 58, "en": "The Referee Panel for each bout shall consist of one Referee, four Judges and one Match Supervisor.", "fr": "Le panel d'arbitres pour chaque combat sera composé d'un arbitre, de quatre juges et d'un superviseur de combat.", "es": "El Panel de Arbitraje para cada encuentro estará compuesto por un árbitro, cuatro jueces y un supervisor del encuentro.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 4.1.1 (omits Score Supervisor)"}, {"num": 59, "en": "If after the bout has started, an Athlete is found not to be wearing a gum - shield, the Athlete will be disqualified.", "fr": "Si, après le début du combat, un athlète s'avère ne pas porter de protège -dents, l'athlète sera disqualifié.", "es": "Si una vez comenzado el combate se descubre que un atleta no lleva puesto el protector dental, el atleta será descalificado.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.14 (2-minute correction period, not automatic disqualification)"}, {"num": 60, "en": "The Referee will give all commands and make all announcements.", "fr": "L'arbitre donnera tous les ordres et fera toutes les annonces.", "es": "El árbitro dará todas las órdenes y hará todos los anuncios.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.3.1(2)"}, {"num": 61, "en": "Duration of the Kumite bout is 1.5 minutes for under 14 years.", "fr": "La durée du combat de Kumité est de 1,5 minute pour les moins de 14 ans.", "es": "La duración del combate de Kumite es de 1,5 minutos para menores de 14 años.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 5.1"}, {"num": 62, "en": "If three Judges signal a score for AKA, the Referee must stop the bout even if he believes they are mistaken.", "fr": "Si trois juges signalent un score pour AKA, l'arbitre doit arrêter le combat même s'il croit qu'ils se trompent.", "es": "Si tres jueces señalan una puntuación para AKA, el árbitro debe parar el combate, incluso si cree que están equivocados.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.1.1"}, {"num": 63, "en": "If two or more Judges signal a score for the same Athlete, the Referee must stop the bout.", "fr": "Si deux uges ou plus signalent un score pour le même athlète, l'arbitre doit arrêter le combat.", "es": "Si dos o más jueces señalan una puntuación para el mismo atleta, el árbitro debe parar el combate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.1.1"}, {"num": 64, "en": "The timing of a bout starts when the Referee gives the signal to start and stops when the Referee calls \"YAME\" or when the time is up.", "fr": "Le chronométrage d'un combat commence lorsque l'arbitre donne le signal du départ et s'arrête lorsque l'arbitre annonce \"YAME\" ou lorsque le temps est écoulé.", "es": "El tiempo de un combate comienza cuando el árbitro da la señal de comienzo y se detiene cuando el árbitro dice \"YAME\" o cuando se acaba el tiempo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 5.3 (omits electronic-signal stopping condition)"}, {"num": 65, "en": "The Referee Panel shall consist of one Referee, four Judges, one Match Supervisor and one Score Keeper.", "fr": "Le panel d'arbitrage sera composé d'un arbitre, de quatre juges, d'un superviseur de combat et d'un marqueur.", "es": "El Panel de Arbitraje estará compuesto por un árbitro, cuatro jueces, un supervisor del encuentro y un anotador de puntuación.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 4.1.1 (Score Supervisor, not 'Score Keeper')"}, {"num": 66, "en": "The Athlete's Coach is the only one allowed to make a protest.", "fr": "Seul l'entraîneur d'athlète est autorisé à faire une protestation.", "es": "El entrenador del atleta es el único autorizado para presentar una protesta.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 13.1.2 (Coach OR official representative)"}, {"num": 67, "en": "If the Referee does not hear the time - up signal, KANSA will blow the whistle.", "fr": "Si l'arbitre n'entend pas le signal de fin de temps, KANSA du combat sifflera.", "es": "Si el árbitro no oye la señal de finalización del tiempo, KANSA del encuentro hará sonar el silbato.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.6.2 (Score-Supervisor, not KANSA)"}, {"num": 68, "en": "The Athletes must only bow properly to each other at the start of the bout.", "fr": "Les athlètes doivent uniquement se saluer correctement au début du combat.", "es": "Los atletas sólo deben saludarse correctamente al comienzo del combate.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.4 (start AND end)"}, {"num": 69, "en": "In individual bouts an Athlete who withdraws voluntarily from the bout is declared KIKEN and an extra eight points are awarded to the opponent.", "fr": "Dans les combats individuels, un athlète qui abandonne volontairement le combat est déclaré KIKEN et huit points supplémentaires sont accordés à l'adversaire.", "es": "En encuentros individuales, un atleta que se retire voluntariamente del combate será declarado KIKEN y se otorgarán ocho puntos extra al oponente.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 6.2 (8 pts is Team rule; Individual Round-robin is 4-0)"}, {"num": 70, "en": "Awareness is the state of continued commitment, which endures after the technique has landed.", "fr": "L’état de conscience est un état d'engagement constant qui perdure une fois que la technique a été mise en œuvre.", "es": "La conciencia de estar a riesgo es el estado de compromiso continuo, que perdura después de que la técnica se haya ejecutado.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.5(4)"}, {"num": 71, "en": "If the organizer has a check -up of equipment before line -up, it is still KANSA's responsibility to ensure that the equipment is in accordance with the rules.", "fr": "Si l'organisateur fait vérifier l'équipement avant l'alignement, il est toujours de la responsabilité du KANSA de s'assurer que l'équipement est conforme aux règles.", "es": "Si el organizador realiza una revisión del equipo antes de la alineación, sigue siendo responsabilidad de KANSA asegurarse de que el equipo es conforme al reglamento.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.10"}, {"num": 72, "en": "An Athlete who stays within the competition area can score on an Athlete outside the competition area.", "fr": "Un athlète qui reste dans la zone de combat peut marquer sur un athlète en dehors de la zone de combat.", "es": "Un atleta que permanezca dentro del área de competición puede puntuar a un atleta fuera del área de competición.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.3"}, {"num": 73, "en": "ATO SHIBARAKU means \"15 seconds of bout time remaining\".", "fr": "ATO SHIBARAKU signifie \"15 secondes de temps de combat restant\".", "es": "ATO SHIBARAKU significa \"quedan 15 segundos de combate\".", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Appendix 1 (Terminology) / Art. 5.4"}, {"num": 74, "en": "ATO SHIBARAKU means \"10 seconds of bout time remaining\".", "fr": "ATO SHIBARAKU signifie \"10 secondes de temps de combat restant\".", "es": "ATO SHIBARAKU significa \"quedan 10 segundos de combate\".", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Appendix 1 (it's 15 seconds)"}, {"num": 75, "en": "A \"skin touch\" to the throat is allowed only in Senior competition.", "fr": "Un \"skin touch\" à la gorge n'est autorisé qu'en compétition senior.", "es": "Un \"skin touch\" en la garganta sólo está permitido en la competición Senior.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.8 (no contact allowed to throat in any category)"}, {"num": 76, "en": "If there are no points at the end of a bout in team matches the Referee will call for HANTEI.", "fr": "S'il n'y a pas de points à la fin d'un combat dans les combats par équipe, l'arbitre demandera HANTEI.", "es": "Si no hay puntos al final de un combate por equipos, el árbitro pedirá HANTEI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.4 / 12.2.6 (HIKIWAKE unless it's the extra bout)"}, {"num": 77, "en": "If an Athlete has been asked before the bout starts, and confirms wearing a groin guard, and it later proves that this is not so, the Athlete will receive a warning or penalty for MUBOBI.", "fr": "Si, avant le début du combat, on demande à un athlète s'il porte un coquille et qu'il confirme que oui, mais qu'il s'avère par la suite que ce n'est pas le cas, l'athlète se verra infliger un avertissement ou une pénalité pour MUBOBI.", "es": "Si se le pregunta a un atleta antes de que comience el combate si lleva protector inguinal y este lo confirma, pero posteriormente se comprueba que no es así, el atleta recibirá una advertencia o una sanción por MUBOBI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.14 (that scenario results in SHIKKAKU, not MUBOBI)"}, {"num": 78, "en": "An Athlete can be penalised for exaggeration even if there is an actual injury.", "fr": "Un athlète peut être pénalisé pour exagération même s'il y a une blessure réelle.", "es": "Un atleta puede ser penalizado por exageración incluso si exista una lesión real.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.4"}, {"num": 79, "en": "The Referee declares the winner, \"AO (AKA) NO KACHI\", and if necessary, breaks the tie in case of HANTEI.", "fr": "L'arbitre déclare le vainqueur, \"AO (AKA) NO KACHI\", et si nécessaire, brise l'égalité en cas de HANTEI.", "es": "El árbitro declarará al ganador ‘’AO (AKA) NO KACHI\", y si es necesario, desempatará en caso de HANTEI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.9"}, {"num": 80, "en": "In the event of a tied score at the end of an inconclusive bout the the Referee and the four Judges will decide the bout by HANTEI.", "fr": "En cas d'égalité des points à la fin d'un combat non concluant, l'arbitre et les quatre juges décideront du combat par HANTEI.", "es": "En caso de empate al final de un combate no concluyente, el árbitro y los cuatro jueces decidirán el combate por HANTEI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.9"}, {"num": 81, "en": "If the Referee Panel has made a decision not in accordance with the Rules of Competition, KANSA will immediately blow his whistle.", "fr": "Si le panel d'arbitres a pris une décision non conforme aux règles de compétition, KANSA sifflera immédiatement.", "es": "Si el panel de arbitraje haya tomado una decisión que no esté de acuerdo con el Reglamento de Competición, KANSA hará sonar inmediatamente su silbato.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.1"}, {"num": 82, "en": "An Athlete should not be penalized for being winded (loss of breath as a consequence of a technique) or simply reacting to an impact even if the technique merited a point by the opponent.", "fr": "Un athlète ne doit pas être pénalisé pour avoir été essoufflé (perte de souffle suite à une technique) ou simplement avoir réagi à un impact même si la technique a valu un point à l'adversaire.", "es": "Un atleta no debe ser penalizado por estar sin aliento (pérdida de aliento como consecuencia de una técnica) o simplemente por reaccionar a un impacto, incluso si la técnica mereció un punto por parte del oponente.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.7"}, {"num": 83, "en": "In team matches, there is no extra bout.", "fr": "Dans les combats par équipe, il n'y a pas de combat supplémentaire.", "es": "En los encuentros por equipos no hay combate extra.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.5.2"}, {"num": 84, "en": "Only the first correctly executed technique of a combination will score.", "fr": "Seule la première technique d'une combinaison correctement exécutée comptera.", "es": "Sólo puntuará la primera técnica correctamente ejecutada de una combinación.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.3 (combination = highest-scoring technique, not first)"}, {"num": 85, "en": "Athletes that appear at the competition area with unauthorized equipment or irregular Karate Gi, will be given one minute to correct the attire.", "fr": "Les athlètes qui se présentent à l'aire de compétition avec un équipement non autorisé ou un Karate Gi irrégulier auront une minute pour corriger leur tenue.", "es": "A los atletas que se presenten en el área de competición con equipamiento no autorizado o un Karate Gi irregular, se les dará un minuto para corregir el atuendo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.14 (two minutes, not one)"}, {"num": 86, "en": "Athletes that are winded as a result of an impact, should be allowed time to catch their breath before the bout is resumed.", "fr": "Les athlètes qui sont essoufflés à la suite d'un impact devraient avoir le temps de reprendre leur souffle avant que le combat ne reprenne.", "es": "A los atletas que estén sin aliento como resultado de un impacto se les debe dar tiempo para recuperar el aliento antes de reanudar el combate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.3 / 8.7"}, {"num": 87, "en": "JODAN is described as the shoulders and the area above the collarbones.", "fr": "JODAN est décrit comme les épaules et la zone au -dessus des clavicules.", "es": "JODAN se describe como los hombros y la zona por encima de la clavícula.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.4 (shoulder junction is excluded from scoring area)"}, {"num": 88, "en": "IPPON is awarded for JODAN kicks or any techniques against an opponent whose any part of the body other than the feet is in contact with the Tatami.", "fr": "IPPON est accordé pour les coups de pied JODAN ou toute technique contre un adversaire dont une partie du corps autre que les pieds est en contact avec le tatami.", "es": "IPPON se concede por patadas JODAN o cualquier técnica contra un oponente cuya cualquier parte del cuerpo, que no sean los pies, esté en contacto con el tatami.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.6 (omits HIZA GAMAE exception)"}, {"num": 89, "en": "HANSOKU CHUI will be given for feigning of injury.", "fr": "HANSOKU CHUI sera donné pour simulation d'une blessure.", "es": "Se concederá HANSOKU CHUI por fingir una lesión.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.5 (minimum is CHUI; HANSOKU CHUI only for obvious display)"}, {"num": 90, "en": "HANSOKU will be given for the first instance of exaggerating an injury.", "fr": "HANSOKU sera donné pour la première exagération d'une blessure.", "es": "Se dará HANSOKU por el primer caso de exageración de una lesión.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.4 (first/slight instance is CHUI)"}, {"num": 91, "en": "A loss of breath by the recipient of a CHUDAN technique indicates lack of control.", "fr": "Une perte de souffle chez le destinataire d'une technique CHUDAN indique un manque de contrôle.", "es": "La pérdida de aliento por parte del receptor de una técnica CHUDAN indica falta de control.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.7"}, {"num": 92, "en": "An Athlete can be given HANSOKU directly for exaggerating the effects of injury.", "fr": "Un athlète peut recevoir HANSOKU directement pour avoir exagéré les effets d'une blessure.", "es": "Se puede dar HANSOKU directamente a un atleta por exagerar los efectos de una lesión.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.4"}, {"num": 93, "en": "A technique, even if effective, delivered after an order to suspend or halt the bout willl not score and can result in a penalty being imposed on the offender.", "fr": "Une technique, même efficace, exécutée après un ordre de suspendre ou d'arrêter le combat ne sera pas comptabilisée et pourra entraîner une pénalité au contrevenant.", "es": "Una técnica, incluso si es efectiva, realizada después de una orden de suspender o parar el combate, no será puntuada y puede dar lugar a que se imponga una sanción al infractor.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.11(a) / 9.1.1(4)"}, {"num": 94, "en": "If there is an error in the draw and the wrong Athletes compete, this cannot be changed afterwards.", "fr": "S'il y a une erreur dans le tirage au sort et que les mauvais athlètes concourent, cela ne peut pas être changé par la suite.", "es": "Si hay un error en el sorteo y compiten los atletas equivocados, esto no podrá cambiarse posteriormente.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.6.7 (bout/match declared null and void)"}, {"num": 95, "en": "Correctly executed techniques landed at the moment the time runs out are valid.", "fr": "Les techniques correctement exécutées au moment où le temps est écoulé sont valides.", "es": "Una técnica eficaz realizada al mismo tiempo que el final del combate es válida.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.10"}, {"num": 96, "en": "If an Athlete is injured and it is considered to be their own fault (MUBOBI), the Referee will decline to give a warning or penalty to the opponent.", "fr": "Si un athlète est blessé et que cela est considéré comme étant de sa faute MUBOBI, l'arbitre refusera de donner un avertissement ou une pénalité à l'adversaire.", "es": "Si un atleta se lesiona y se considera que es por su propia culpa (MUBOBI), el árbitro declinará dar una advertencia o penalización al oponente.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.2 / 10.4.14"}, {"num": 97, "en": "KANSA has no vote or authority in matters of judgments, such as whether a score was valid or not, unless there has been an error in the application of the rules.", "fr": "KANSA n'a ni droit de vote ni pouvoir de décision en matière de jugement, par exemple pour déterminer si un score est valable ou non, sauf en cas d'erreur dans l'application des règles.", "es": "KANSA no tiene voto ni autoridad en cuestiones de juicios tales como si una puntuación ha sido válida o no, a menos que haya habido un error en la aplicación de las reglas.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.5(2)"}, {"num": 98, "en": "YUKO is always awarded for punches on the back.", "fr": "YUKO est toujours attribué pour les coups portés dans le dos.", "es": "YUKO siempre se concede por técnicas de puño en la espalda.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.4 (scoring area not defined to include the back; not 'always')"}, {"num": 99, "en": "\"Skin touch\" is allowed in all official categories.", "fr": "\"Skin touch\" est autorisé dans toutes les catégories officielles.", "es": "\"Skin touch\" está permitido en todas las categorías oficiales.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.9"}, {"num": 100, "en": "An Athlete who does not obey the Referee's orders will be given SHIKKAKU.", "fr": "Un athlète qui n'obéit pas aux ordres de l'arbitre se verra attribuer SHIKKAKU.", "es": "Un atleta que no obedezca las órdenes del árbitro recibirá SHIKKAKU.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.17"}, {"num": 101, "en": "The Score Supervisor will order the Referee to halt the bout if there is a contravention of the rules.", "fr": "Le superviseur du score ordonnera à l'arbitre d'arrêter le combat s'il y a une infraction aux règles.", "es": "El supervisor de puntuación ordenará al árbitro detener el combate si hay una contravención del reglas.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.1 (that's KANSA's duty, not Score Supervisor's)"}, {"num": 102, "en": "If in a combination, the first technique merits a YUKO and the second merits a penalty, both shall be given.", "fr": "Si dans une combinaison, la première technique mérite un YUKO et la seconde une pénalité, les deux seront accordées.", "es": "Si en una combinación la primera técnica merece un YUKO y la segunda merece una penalización, se darán ambas.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.11(f)"}, {"num": 103, "en": "\"Skin touch\" is defined as touching the target without transferring energy into the protective helmet or head of the Athlete.", "fr": "On entend par \"skin touch\" le fait de toucher la cible sans transmettre d'énergie au casque ou à la tête de l'athlète.", "es": "\"Skin touch\" se define como un contacto con el objetivo sin transferir energía a el casco o la cabeza del atleta.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.9"}, {"num": 104, "en": "It is not possible to score while lying on the floor.", "fr": "Il n'est pas possible de marquer en étant allongé sur le sol.", "es": "No es posible marcar estando tumbado en el suelo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.10(f) (follow-up scoring after a fall is contemplated)"}, {"num": 105, "en": "An Athlete not wearing the WKF approved equipment will be given two minutes to change for the approved type.", "fr": "Un athlète ne portant pas l'équipement approuvé par la WKF aura deux minutes pour se changer pour l’équipement approuvé.", "es": "Un atleta que no lleve el equipo aprobado por la WKF dispondrá de dos minutos para cambiarlo por el tipo aprobado.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.14"}, {"num": 106, "en": "An Athlete injured in Kumite and withdrawn under the ten -second rule cannot compete in the Kata competition.", "fr": "Un athlète blessé en Kumité et retiré selon la règle des dix secondes ne peut pas participer à la compétition de Kata.", "es": "Un atleta lesionado en Kumite y retirado bajo la regla de los diez segundos no podrá competir en la competición de Kata.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.2.4 (withdrawn from Kumite events only)"}, {"num": 107, "en": "An injured Athlete who has been declared unfit to fight by the Tournament Doctor cannot fight again in that competition.", "fr": "Un athlète blessé qui a été déclaré inapte au combat par le médecin du tournoi ne peut plus combattre dans cette compétition.", "es": "Un atleta lesionado que haya sido declarado no apto para combatir por el médico del torneo no podrá volver a combatir en esa competición.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.1.1 (can resume with tournament doctor's permission)"}, {"num": 108, "en": "If an Athlete behaves badly on the competition area after the end of the bout or match, the Referee can still give SHIKKAKU.", "fr": "Si un athlète se comporte mal sur l'aire de compétition après la fin du combat ou du combat, l'arbitre peut toujours accorder SHIKKAKU.", "es": "Si un atleta se comporta mal en el área de competición después del final del encuentro o combate, el árbitro aún puede dar SHIKKAKU.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.17"}, {"num": 109, "en": "KANSA has a vote in cases of SHIKKAKU.", "fr": "KANSA a un vote en cas de SHIKKAKU.", "es": "KANSA tiene voto en los casos de SHIKKAKU.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.5(2)"}, {"num": 110, "en": "In Male team matches if a team wins three bouts, then the match is over at that point.", "fr": "Dans les rencontres par équipes masculines, si une équipe gagne trois combats, la rencontre prend fin à ce moment-là.", "es": "En combates por equipos masculinos, si un equipo gana tres combates, entonces el combate finaliza en ese momento.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.5.1 / 12.5.4"}, {"num": 111, "en": "In Female team matches if a team wins two bouts, then the match is over at that point.", "fr": "Dans les rencontres par équipes féminines, si une équipe gagne deux combats, la rencontre prend fin à ce moment -là.", "es": "En los combates por equipos femeninos, si un equipo gana dos combates, el combate finalizará en ese momento.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.5.2 / 12.5.4"}, {"num": 112, "en": "If an Athlete seizes the opponent and does not perform an immediate technique or throw the Referee will call \"YAME\".", "fr": "Si un athlète saisit l'adversaire et n'exécute pas une technique immédiate ou une projection, l'arbitre annoncera \"YAME\".", "es": "Si un atleta agarra al oponente y no realiza una técnica o derribo inmediato, el árbitro anunciara \"YAME\".", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.10(e)"}, {"num": 113, "en": "An Athlete who commits an act which harms the prestige and honour of Karate -Do will be given HANSOKU.", "fr": "Un athlète qui commet un acte portant atteinte au prestige et à l'honneur du Karate -Do se verra infliger un HANSOKU.", "es": "Un atleta que cometa un acto que dañe el prestigio y el honor del Karate -Do será sancionado con HANSOKU.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.1 (that's a SHIKKAKU ground, not HANSOKU)"}, {"num": 114, "en": "If an action of an Athlete is considered to be dangerous and deliberately violates the rules concerning prohibited behaviour, the Athlete will be given SHIKKAKU.", "fr": "Si le comportement d'un athlète est jugé dangereux et enfreint délibérément les règles relatives aux comportements interdits, l'athlète se verra infliger un SHIKKAKU.", "es": "Si una acción de un atleta se considere peligrosa e infrinja deliberadamente las reglas relativas al comportamiento prohibido, se dará al atleta SHIKKAKU.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.1 / 9.1.1(14) (not automatically SHIKKAKU)"}, {"num": 115, "en": "Correctly executed techniques after the time-up signal are valid.", "fr": "Les techniques correctement exécutées après le signal de fin de temps sont valables.", "es": "Las técnicas correctamente ejecutadas después de la señal de tiempo son válidas.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.11(a)"}, {"num": 116, "en": "Correctly executed techniques upon or after \"WAKARETE\" are valid.", "fr": "Les techniques exécutées correctement au moment du \"WAKARETE\" ou après sont valables.", "es": "Las técnicas ejecutadas correctamente durante o después de \"WAKARETE\" son válidas.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.11(b)"}, {"num": 117, "en": "At HANTEI, if three Judges signal victory for AKA and the fourth Judge signals victory for AO, the Referee must give victory for AKA.", "fr": "Chez HANTEI, si trois juges désignent AKA comme vainqueur et que le quatrième juge désigne AO comme vainqueur, l'arbitre doit déclarer AKA vainqueur.", "es": "En HANTEI, si tres jueces señalan la victoria para AKA y el cuarto juez señala la victoria para AO, el árbitro debe dar la victoria a AKA.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.7 / 15.3.1(10)"}, {"num": 118, "en": "Passivity cannot be given to an Athlete having a lead by points or SENSHU.", "fr": "La passivité ne peut être accordée à un athlète qui mène au score ou au SENSHU.", "es": "No se puede dar pasividad a un atleta que tenga ventaja por punto o SENSHU.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.1(10)"}, {"num": 119, "en": "Only the Coach designated for the specific bout is allowed to guide the Athlete from the place allocated to the Coach close to the competition area.", "fr": "Seul l'entraîneur désigné pour le combat en question est autorisé à guider l'athlète depuis la place qui lui est réservée à proximité de l'aire de compétition.", "es": "Sólo el entrenador designado para el combate específico puede guiar al atleta desde el lugar asignado al entrenador cerca del área de competición.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.5"}, {"num": 120, "en": "If an Athlete does not regain his or her feet within ten seconds, the Referee will announce \"KIKEN\" and \"KACHI\" to the opponent.", "fr": "Si un athlète ne se remet pas sur ses pieds dans les dix secondes, l'arbitre annoncera \"KIKEN\" et \"KACHI\" à l'adversaire.", "es": "Si un atleta no se recupera en diez segundos, el árbitro anunciará \"KIKEN\" y \"KACHI\" al oponente.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.2.4 / 6.1 / 6.5"}, {"num": 121, "en": "If an Athlete is thrown and lands partly outside the competition area, the Referee will immediately call \"YAME\".", "fr": "Si un athlète est projeté et atterrit en partie hors de l'aire de combat, l'arbitre prononce immédiatement \"YAME\".", "es": "Si un atleta es derribado y cae parcialmente fuera del área de competición, el árbitro anunciará inmediatamente \"YAME\".", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.10(a),(f) (follow-up chance allowed, not immediate)"}, {"num": 122, "en": "The Athlete is not allowed to signal to the Coach to request a video review.", "fr": "L'athlète n'a pas le droit de faire signe à l'entraîneur pour demander une révision vidéo.", "es": "El atleta no podrá señalar al entrenador el deseo de que solicite una revisión de vídeo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.7 / 14.4"}, {"num": 123, "en": "The Athlete should be examined outside the Tatami.", "fr": "L'athlète doit être examiné en dehors du tatami.", "es": "El atleta debe ser examinado fuera del tatami.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.2.2 / 11.2.4 (10-second rule allows on-mat examination)"}, {"num": 124, "en": "KANSA has to blow the whistle if the Judges are holding the joysticks in the wrong hands.", "fr": "KANSA doit siffler si les juges tiennent les joysticks dans les mauvaises mains.", "es": "KANSA tiene que hacer sonar el silbato si los jueces están sujetando los joysticks en las manos equivocadas.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.4(17)"}, {"num": 125, "en": "Gum -shields are obligatory for all Kumite Athletes.", "fr": "Le port d'un protège -dents est obligatoire pour tous les atlètes de Kumite.", "es": "Los protectores bucales son obligatorios para todos los atletas de Kumite.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.7(b)"}, {"num": 126, "en": "After a throw the Referee will allow a maximum of two seconds for a score to be made.", "fr": "Après un lancer, l'arbitre accordera un délai maximal de deux secondes pour marquer un point.", "es": "Después de un derribo, el árbitro permitirá un máximo de dos segundos para que se realice una puntuación.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "No such provision in the Rules"}, {"num": 127, "en": "If an Athlete scores with a strong kick and propels the opponent out of the area, the Referee should award WAZA -ARI and give the opponent a warning or penalty for JOGAI.", "fr": "Si un athlète marque un point grâce à un puissant coup de pied et repousse son adversaire hors de la zone, l'arbitre doit accorder un WAZA -ARI et infliger à l'adversaire un avertissement ou une pénalité pour JOGAI.", "es": "Si un atleta puntúa con una fuerte patada e impulsa al oponente fuera del área, el árbitro deberá conceder WAZA -ARI y dar al oponente una advertencia o penalización por JOGAI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.13 (no JOGAI - pushed out by opponent exception)"}, {"num": 128, "en": "If an official protest is lodged the ensuing bouts must be delayed until the result of the protest is given.", "fr": "Si une protestation officielle est déposée, les combats suivants doivent être retardés jusqu'à ce que le résultat de la protestation soit donné.", "es": "Si se presenta una protesta oficial, los encuentros siguientes deben retrasarse hasta que se dé el resultado de la protesta.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 13.1.4 / 13.1.5 (only rounds involving the affected Athletes)"}, {"num": 129, "en": "If the Referee awards a point for a technique which has caused injury KANSA should signal for the bout to be stopped.", "fr": "Si l'arbitre accorde un point pour une technique qui a causé une blessure, KANSA doit signaler l'arrêt du combat.", "es": "Si el árbitro conceda un punto por una técnica que haya causado lesión, KANSA deberá indicar que se detenga el encuentro.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.4 (not a listed KANSA-whistle trigger); Art. 11.2.1"}, {"num": 130, "en": "If the Referee fails to hear the time -up bell, the Scorekeeper should whistle.", "fr": "Si l'arbitre n'entend pas la cloche de fin de temps, le chronométreur doit siffler.", "es": "Si el árbitro no oye la señal de final de tiempo, el anotador de puntuación hará sonar su silbato.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.6.2 (Score-Supervisor, not Scorekeeper)"}, {"num": 131, "en": "WAKARETE for breaking up a clinch can be given at any time of the bout.", "fr": "WAKARETE pour séparer les adversaires lorsqu'ils sont enlacés, peut être donné à tout moment du combat.", "es": "Para romper un clinch en cualquier momento del combate se puede dar WAKARETE.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.1.2 / 10.1.4"}, {"num": 132, "en": "FUKUSHIN SHUGO is obligatory before imposing SHIKKAKU.", "fr": "Il faut d'abord exécuter FUKUSHIN SHUGO avant d'accorder SHIKKAKU.", "es": "FUKUSHIN SHUGO es obligatorio para poder dar SHIKKAKU.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.4"}, {"num": 133, "en": "If an Athlete is injured during a bout and needs medical treatment three minutes will be given in which to receive it, after that the Referee will decide whether the Athlete should be declared unfit to fight or whether more time should be given.", "fr": "Si un athlète est blessé pendant un combat et a besoin d'un traitement médical, trois minutes seront accordées pour le recevoir, après quoi l'arbitre décidera si l’athlète sera déclaré inapte au combat ou si plus de temps sera accordé.", "es": "Si un atleta resulta lesionado durante un combate y necesite tratamiento médico, se le concederán tres minutos para recibirlo, tras los cuales el árbitro decidirá si el atleta será declarado no apto para combatir o si se le concederá más tiempo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.2.3"}, {"num": 134, "en": "An Athlete who exits the competition area (JOGAI) with less than 15 seconds of bout time remaining will be given a minimum of CHUI.", "fr": "Un athlète qui quitte l'aire de combat (JOGAI) alors qu'il reste moins de 15 secondes, se verra infliger au minimum une pénalité CHUI.", "es": "A un atleta que salga del área (JOGAI) con menos de 15 segundos de combate restantes, se le dará un mínimo de CHUI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.16 (could be minimum HANSOKU CHUI if deemed avoiding combat)"}, {"num": 135, "en": "To correct a score given to the wrong Athlete, the Referee should turn towards the Athlete given the score in error, make the sign of TORIMASEN, and then give the score to the opponent.", "fr": "Pour corriger un score donné au mauvais athlète, l'arbitre doit se tourner vers l’athlète ayant reçu le score par erreur, faire le signe de TORIMASEN, puis donner le score à l'adversaire.", "es": "Para corregir una puntuación dada al atleta equivocado, el árbitro debe girarse hacia el atleta al que se le ha dado la puntuación por error, hacer el signo de TORIMASEN, y después dar la puntuación al oponente.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.4(4) (KANSA corrects it; no such Referee self-correction sequence described)"}, {"num": 136, "en": "If an Athlete scores with a well - controlled CHUDAN kick, then accidentally punches his opponent in the face causing a slight injury, WAZA - ARI and a warning should be given.", "fr": "Si un athlète marque avec un CHUDAN kick bien contrôlé, puis frappe accidentellement son adversaire au visage causant une légère blessure, WAZA -ARI et un avertissement doivent être donnés.", "es": "Si un atleta puntúa con una patada CHUDAN bien controlada y, después, accidentalmente golpea a su oponente en la cara causándole una herida leve, se debe dar WAZA -ARI y una advertencia.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.6 / 10.4.2"}, {"num": 137, "en": "If an injured Athlete has been given medical treatment and the Official Doctor says that the Athlete can continue fighting the Referee cannot overrule the Doctor's decision.", "fr": "Si un combattant blessé a reçu un traitement médical et le médecin officiel dit que le combattant peut continuer à se battre, l'arbitre ne peut pas annuler la décision du médecin.", "es": "Si un atleta lesionado ha recibido tratamiento médico y el médico oficial dice que el atleta puede continuar combatiendo, el árbitro no puede invalidar la decisión del médico.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.2.5"}, {"num": 138, "en": "The Referee can stop the bout even if the Judges do not signal.", "fr": "L'arbitre peut arrêter le combat même si les juges ne le signalent pas.", "es": "El árbitro puede detener el combate incluso si los jueces no lo señalan.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.10"}, {"num": 139, "en": "Once WAKARETE is called by the Referee the Coaches do not have the opportunity to make a video review request unless the techniques happened before WAKARETE was called.", "fr": "Une fois que l'arbitre a prononcé WAKARETE, les entraîneurs n'ont plus la possibilité de demander une révision vidéo, sauf si les technique ont été exécutées avant que WAKARETE ne soit prononcé.", "es": "Una vez que el árbitro anuncia WAKARETE, los entrenadores no tienen la oportunidad de solicitar una revisión de vídeo, a menos que las técnicas se hayan producido antes de que se anuncie WAKARETE.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 14.16"}, {"num": 140, "en": "\"Avoiding Combat\" refers to a situation where an Athlete attempts to prevent the opponent from having the opportunity to score by using time - wasting behaviour.", "fr": "\"Eviter le combat\" fait référence à une situation dans laquelle un athlète tente d'empêcher l'adversaire d'avoir la possibilité de marquer en utilisant un comportement de perte de temps.", "es": "\"Evitar el combate\" se refiere a una situación en la que un atleta intenta evitar que el oponente tenga la oportunidad de puntuar utilizando un comportamiento de pérdida de tiempo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.16"}, {"num": 141, "en": "TSUZUKETE, unless preceded by WAKARETE, is not used if there is less than 15 seconds left of the bout.", "fr": "TSUZUKETE, sauf s'il est précédé de WAKARETE, n'est pas utilisé s'il reste moins de 15 secondes du combat.", "es": "TSUZUKETE, a menos que vaya precedido de WAKARETE, no se utiliza si quedan menos de 15 segundos de combate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.1.4"}, {"num": 142, "en": "In team matches if two Athletes injure each other and are unable to continue, and the score is equal, the Referee will announce HIKIWAKE.", "fr": "Dans les rencontres par équipes, si deux athlètes se blessent l'un l'autre et ne peuvent pas continuer, et si le score est égal, l'arbitre annoncera HIKIWAKE.", "es": "En encuentros por equipos, si dos atletas se lesionan mutuamente y no pueden continuar y la puntuación es igual, el árbitro anunciará HIKIWAKE.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.3 / 12.2.4"}, {"num": 143, "en": "if there are less than 15 seconds of bout time remaining and a losing Athlete, desperately trying to equalise, exits the area (JOGAI) the Athlete will be given a minimum of HANSOKU CHUI.", "fr": "S'il reste moins de 15 secondes de combat et qu'un athlète perdant, essayant désespérément d'égaliser, sort de l'aire de compétition (JOGAI), l'athlète recevra un minimum de HANSOKU CHUI.", "es": "Si quedan menos de 15 segundos de combate y el atleta que va perdiendo, intentando desesperadamente igualar, se sale del área (JOGAI), se le dará un mínimo de HANSOKU CHUI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.16 (desperately attacking is not 'avoiding combat')"}, {"num": 144, "en": "Techniques which land below the belt cannot score.", "fr": "Les techniques portées sous la ceinture ne comptent pas.", "es": "Las técnicas realizadas por debajo del cinturón no pueden puntuar.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.4 / 9.1.1(2)"}, {"num": 145, "en": "Techniques, which land on the shoulder blade, can score.", "fr": "Les techniques qui touchent l'omoplate peuvent marquer.", "es": "Las técnicas que se realicen sobre el omóplato pueden puntuar.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.4 (shoulder-blade junction is excluded)"}, {"num": 146, "en": "If AKA accidentally kicks AO on the hip and AO cannot continue the bout, then AO will be given KIKEN.", "fr": "Si AKA donne accidentellement un coup de pied à AO sur la hanche et que AO ne peut pas continuer le combat, AO recevra un KIKEN.", "es": "Si AKA accidentalmente golpea a AO en la cadera y AO no puede continuar el combate, entonces AO recibirá KIKEN.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 6.1 (injury caused by opponent - not KIKEN grounds)"}, {"num": 147, "en": "If an Athlete is obviously out of breath due to lack of endurance, the Referee should stop the bout to give the Athlete time to recover.", "fr": "Si un athlète est manifestement à bout de souffle en raison d'un manque d'endurance, l'arbitre doit interrompre le combat afin de lui laisser le temps de récupérer.", "es": "Si un atleta está obviamente sin aliento debido a la falta de resistencia, el árbitro deberá detener el combate para darle tiempo a recuperarse.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.10 (fatigue/endurance is not a listed reason to halt)"}, {"num": 148, "en": "An Athlete who establishes a clear lead of eight points is declared the winner.", "fr": "Un athlète qui prend une avance nette de huit points est déclaré vainqueur.", "es": "El atleta que establezca una clara ventaja de ocho puntos será declarado vencedor.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.7"}, {"num": 149, "en": "When time is up, the Athlete who has scored the most points is declared the winner.", "fr": "À la fin du temps imparti, l'athlète ayant marqué le plus de points est déclaré vainqueur.", "es": "Cuando se acabe el tiempo, el atleta que haya obtenido más puntos será declarado ganador.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.8"}, {"num": 150, "en": "An otherwise correctly executed technique will be penalized if executed at the same time as WAKARETE has been called.", "fr": "Une technique correctement exécutée sera pénalisée si elle est exécutée en même temps que l’annonce du WAKARETE.", "es": "Una técnica correctamente ejecutada será penalizada si se ejecuta al mismo tiempo que se ha ordenado WAKARETE.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.1.5 (not penalised)"}, {"num": 151, "en": "There are two degrees of official warnings.", "fr": "Il y a deux degrés d'avertissements officiels.", "es": "Hay dos grados de advertencias oficiales.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.2.1"}, {"num": 152, "en": "CHUI is given, up to three times, for smaller infractions.", "fr": "CHUI est donné, jusqu'à trois fois, pour des infractions mineures.", "es": "CHUI se da, hasta tres veces, por infracciones menores.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.2.1"}, {"num": 153, "en": "HANSOKU CHUI cannot be given if three CHUI have not already been given.", "fr": "On ne peut pas infliger HANSOKU CHUI si trois pénalités CHUI n'ont pas déjà été infligées.", "es": "No se puede dar HANSOKU CHUI si no se han dado ya tres CHUI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.2.1 (can also be given directly for serious infractions)"}, {"num": 154, "en": "A warning or penalty for MUBOBI is only given if an Athlete is hit or injured through their own fault or negligence.", "fr": "Une avertissement ou une sanction pour MUBOBI n'est infligé(e) que si un athlète est touché ou blessé par sa propre faute ou par négligence.", "es": "Una advertencia o penalización por MUBOBI sólo se da cuando un atleta es golpeado o lesionado por su propia culpa o negligencia.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.14"}, {"num": 155, "en": "An Athlete who is hit through their own fault and exaggerates the effect should receive a warning or penalty for MUBOBI or exaggeration but not both.", "fr": "Un athlète qui est touché par sa propre faute et qui en exagère l'effet doit recevoir un avertissement ou une pénalité pour MUBOBI ou pour exagération, mais pas les deux.", "es": "Un atleta que es golpeado por su propia culpa y exagera el efecto debe recibir una advertencia o penalización por MUBOBI o exageración, pero no ambas.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.14 / 10.4.4-10.4.5 (no such exclusivity stated)"}, {"num": 156, "en": "If an Athlete makes a good CHUDAN kick and the opponent catches the leg a score cannot be given.", "fr": "Si un athlète exécute un bon coup de pied CHUDAN et que l'adversaire attrape la jambe, aucun point ne peut être attribué.", "es": "Si un atleta realiza una buena patada CHUDAN y el oponente atrapa la pierna, no se puede dar puntuación.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.5 (valid if criteria met before being caught)"}, {"num": 157, "en": "An Athlete makes a JODAN kick with all six scoring criteria. The opponent puts the hand up to intercept the kick and the hand then lightly hits his own face, the Referee can give IPPON since the kick was not effectively blocked.", "fr": "Un athlète exécute un coup de pied JODAN qui remplit les six critères de notation. L'adversaire lève la main pour intercepter le coup de pied et se touche légèrement le visage avec la main, l'arbitre peut accorder un IPPON, car le coup de pied n'a pas été bloqué efficacement.", "es": "Un atleta realiza una patada JODAN con los seis criterios de puntuación. El oponente levanta la mano para interceptar la patada y entonces la mano golpea ligeramente su propia cara. El árbitro puede dar IPPON, ya que la patada no fue bloqueada eficazmente.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.5 / 8.6"}, {"num": 158, "en": "A male team can compete with only two Athletes.", "fr": "Une équipe masculine peut participer avec seulement deux athlètes.", "es": "Un equipo masculino puede competir con sólo dos atletas.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 3.5.1 (minimum 3 for male teams)"}, {"num": 159, "en": "Authorised advertising for WKF is displayed on the left sleeve of the Karate Gi.", "fr": "La publicité autorisée par WKF figure sur la manche gauche du Karate -Gi.", "es": "La publicidad autorizada de WKF se muestra en la manga izquierda del Karate Gi.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1 (national emblem on left breast; brands on shoulders - not left sleeve)"}, {"num": 160, "en": "National Federations are not allowed to put advertising on the Athlete's Karate Gi.", "fr": "Les fédérations nationales ne sont pas autorisées à mettre de la publicité sur le Karate Gi de l’athlète.", "es": "Las Federaciones Nacionales no están autorizadas a poner publicidad en el Karate Gi del atleta.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.2 (WKF EC can authorise sponsor logos)"}, {"num": 161, "en": "A Kumite Athlete who receives KIKEN cannot compete again in that tournament.", "fr": "Un athlète de Kumite qui reçoit KIKEN ne peut plus participer à ce tournoi.", "es": "Un atleta de Kumite que reciba KIKEN no podrá volver a competir en ese torneo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 6.4 (does not affect another category)"}, {"num": 162, "en": "An extra bout is used only for team matches.", "fr": "Un combat supplémentaire n'est utilisé que pour les combats par équipes.", "es": "Un combate extra se utiliza sólo para encuentros por equipos.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.3.1(9) / 12.5.2 (also used in individual round-robin ties)"}, {"num": 163, "en": "KANSA needs to blow the whistle if the Referee gives a score to an Athlete and MUBOBI to the other.", "fr": "KANSA doit siffler si l'arbitre attribue un score à un athlète et MUBOBI à l'autre.", "es": "KANSA tiene que hacer sonar el silbato si el árbitro da una puntuación a un atleta y MUBOBI al otro.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.4(6)"}, {"num": 164, "en": "Serious violation of conduct, discipline, or malicious behavior merits HANSOKU CHUI.", "fr": "Une violation grave de la conduite, de la discipline ou un comportement malveillant mérite HANSOKU CHUI.", "es": "Una violación grave de la conducta o disciplina o comportamiento malicioso merece HANSOKU CHUI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.3.3 (Disciplinary Commission/EC action, not HANSOKU CHUI)"}, {"num": 165, "en": "In international competitions, the Referee must not have the same nationality as either of the Athletes, although one of the Judges can if both Coaches agree.", "fr": "Dans les compétitions internationales, l'arbitre ne doit pas avoir la même nationalité que l'un des athlètes, mais l'un des juges peut l’avoir si les deux entraîneurs sont d'accord.", "es": "En competiciones internacionales, el árbitro no debe tener la misma nacionalidad que ninguno de los atletas, aunque uno de los jueces puede si ambos entrenadores están de acuerdo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 4.1.2 (applies to all officials, no exception)"}, {"num": 166, "en": "KANSA will line up together with the Referee and the Judges.", "fr": "KANSA s'alignera avec l'arbitre et les juges.", "es": "KANSA se alineará junto con el árbitro y los jueces.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 1.8 / 4.4.1 (KANSA seated at official table, not in the lineup)"}, {"num": 167, "en": "The Coaches will be seated outside the safety area, on their respective sides facing towards the official table.", "fr": "Les entraîneurs seront assis à l'extérieur de la zone de sécurité, chacun de leur côté, face à la table officielle.", "es": "Los entrenadores se sentarán fuera de la zona de seguridad, en sus respectivos lados, mirando hacia la mesa oficial.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 1.10 (exception when TATAMI configuration makes it impractical)"}, {"num": 168, "en": "KANSA does not need to interfere if the Referee gives a score to an Athlete and exaggeration to the other.", "fr": "KANSA n'a pas à intervenir si l'arbitre attribue un point à un athlète et l’exagération à l'autre.", "es": "KANSA no necesita interferir si el árbitro da una puntuación a un atleta y una exageración al otro.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.4(5) (KANSA must whistle in that case)"}, {"num": 169, "en": "In team matches the Referee and the Judges will rotate for each bout - provided that all hold the required license.", "fr": "Dans les combats par équipes, le arbitre et les juges tourne pour chaque combat - à condition que tous soient titulaires de la licence requise.", "es": "En los encuentros por equipos, el árbitro y los jueces rotarán para cada combate, siempre que todos posean la licencia requerida.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 4.4.5"}, {"num": 170, "en": "The Referee can move around the entire Tatami including the safety zones.", "fr": "L'arbitre peut se déplacer sur tout le tatami, y compris dans les zones de sécurité.", "es": "El árbitro puede moverse por todo el tatami, incluidas las zonas de seguridad.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 1.7"}, {"num": 171, "en": "The red and blue belts must be without any personal embroideries or markings.", "fr": "Les ceintures rouges et bleues ne doivent comporter aucune broderie ni aucun marquage personnel.", "es": "Los cinturones rojos y azules deben estar sin bordados o marcas personales.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(c)"}, {"num": 172, "en": "Personal embroidery on the Karate Gi is allowed only in bouts for medals.", "fr": "La broderie personnelle sur le Karate Gi est autorisée seulement dans les combats pour les médailles.", "es": "Los bordados personales en el Karate Gi sólo están permitidos en los combates por medallas.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1 (no such medal-bout exception)"}, {"num": 173, "en": "If contact is considered by the Referee to be strong, but does not diminish the Athlete's chances of winning, a warning (CHUI) can be given.", "fr": "Si l'arbitre considère que le contact est fort, mais qu'il ne diminue pas les chances de victoire du athlète, un avertissement CHUI peut être donné.", "es": "Si el árbitro considera que un contacto es fuerte, pero no disminuye las posibilidades del atleta de ganar, se puede dar una advertencia (CHUI).", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.1"}, {"num": 174, "en": "An obvious overreaction to a contact will receive a CHUI.", "fr": "Une réaction manifestement excessive à un contact sera sanctionnée par un CHUI.", "es": "Una reacción exagerada a un contacto recibirá un CHUI.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.4 (obvious overreaction = HANSOKU CHUI)"}, {"num": 175, "en": "Judges cannot indicate a score before the Referee stops the bout.", "fr": "Les juges ne peuvent pas attribuer de score avant que l'arbitre n'ait arrêté le combat.", "es": "Los jueces no pueden indicar una puntuación antes de que el árbitro detenga el combate.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.4.1(1) / 12.1.1 (Judges signal first, prompting the Referee to stop)"}, {"num": 176, "en": "An obvious display of exaggeration will receive HANSOKU.", "fr": "Toute exagération manifeste sera sanctionnée par HANSOKU.", "es": "Una muestra obvia de exageración recibirá HANSOKU.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.4 (obvious display = HANSOKU CHUI)"}, {"num": 177, "en": "Any instance of feigning an injury, however slight, will receive a minimum warning of CHUI.", "fr": "Tout cas de simulation d'une blessure, aussi légère soit -elle, donnera lieu à un avertissement de niveau CHUI au minimum.", "es": "Cualquier caso de fingir una lesión, por leve que sea, recibirá una advertencia mínima de CHUI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.5"}, {"num": 178, "en": "An obvious display of any feigning such as staggering around, falling on the floor, standing up and falling down again, and so on, will receive SHIKKAKU directly.", "fr": "Toute simulation manifeste, telle que tituber, tomber par terre, se relever puis retomber, et ainsi de suite, sera directement sanctionnée par un SHIKKAKU.", "es": "Una muestra obvia de cualquier fingimiento, como tambalearse, caerse al suelo, levantarse y volver a caerse, etc., recibirá directamente SHIKKAKU.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.5"}, {"num": 179, "en": "Any feigning of an injury from a technique that in fact has been determined by the Judges as a point will as a minimum result in HANSOKU CHUI.", "fr": "Toute simulation d'une blessure suite à une technique qui a en réalité été jugée valable par les juges entraînera au minimum HANSOKU CHUI.", "es": "Cualquier fingimiento de lesión de una técnica que haya sido determinada por los jueces como un punto, resultará como mínimo en HANSOKU CHUI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.5"}, {"num": 180, "en": "If an Athlete scores with more than one consecutive technique before YAME, the Judges must show the higher score regardless of which sequence the techniques scored.", "fr": "Si un athlète marque avec plus d'une technique consécutive avant YAME, les juges doivent montrer le point le plus élevé, indépendamment de la séquence des techniques marquées.", "es": "Si un atleta puntúa con más de una técnica consecutiva antes de YAME, los jueces deben mostrar el punto más alto, independientemente de la secuencia en que las técnicas hayan puntuado.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.3"}, {"num": 181, "en": "In team matches, if after the extra bout there are no scores, or it is equal scores with no SENSHU, the bout will be decided by HANTEI.", "fr": "Dans les rencontres par équipe, si après le combat supplémentaire il n'y a pas de score, ou s'il y a égalité de score sans SENSHU, le résultat de la rencontre sera décidée par HANTEI.", "es": "En encuentros por equipos, si después del combate extra no hay puntuación o hay igualdad de puntuación sin SENSHU, el encuentro se decidirá por HANTEI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.5.3"}, {"num": 182, "en": "JOGAI occurs when an Athlete exits from the competition area, and it is not caused by the opponent.", "fr": "JOGAI se produit lorsqu'un athlète sort de l'aire de compétition et que ce n'est pas causé par l'adversaire.", "es": "JOGAI se produce cuando un atleta sale del área de competición y no es causado por el adversario.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.13"}, {"num": 183, "en": "The minimum warning for running away, avoiding combat and/or time - wasting during ATO SHIBARAKU is HANSOKU CHUI.", "fr": "L'avertissement minimum en cas de fuite, éviter le combat et/ou perdre du temps pendant ATO SHIBARAKU est HANSOKU CHUI.", "es": "La advertencia mínima por huir, evitar combate y/o perder tiempo durante ATO SHIBARAKU, es HANSOKU CHUI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.16"}, {"num": 184, "en": "The pivotal point of the throw must not be above the thrower's hip level and the opponent must be held onto throughout, so that a safe landing can be made.", "fr": "Le point d'appui de la projection ne doit pas se situer au -dessus du niveau des hanches du lanceur, et l'adversaire doit être maintenu tout au long du mouvement afin de garantir un atterrissage en toute sécurité.", "es": "El punto de giro del lanzamiento no debe estar por encima del nivel de la cadera del lanzador y el adversario debe ser sujetado en todo momento, de forma que se pueda realizar un aterrizaje seguro.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.8"}, {"num": 185, "en": "Holding the opponent's Karate Gi is not permitted to break a fall.", "fr": "Il est interdit de tenir le karaté -gi de l'adversaire pour amortir une chute.", "es": "No está permitido agarrarse al Karate Gi del adversario para frenar una caída.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.12 (permitted, to break a fall)"}, {"num": 186, "en": "KANSA does not need to interfere if the Referee gives a score for a technique done after the time is up.", "fr": "KANSA n'a pas à intervenir si l'arbitre attribue un point pour une technique effectuée après la fin du temps imparti.", "es": "KANSA no necesita interferir si el árbitro da una puntuación por una técnica realizada una vez finalizado el tiempo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.4(7)"}, {"num": 187, "en": "YUKO is worth one point.", "fr": "YUKO vaut un point.", "es": "YUKO vale un punto.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.6"}, {"num": 188, "en": "WAZA -ARI is worth two points.", "fr": "WAZA -ARI vaut deux points.", "es": "WAZA -ARI vale dos puntos.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.6"}, {"num": 189, "en": "IPPON is worth three points.", "fr": "IPPON vaut trois points.", "es": "IPPON vale tres puntos.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.6"}, {"num": 190, "en": "It is the duty of the Tatami Manager to ensure before each bout or match that the Athletes are wearing the approved equipment.", "fr": "Il est du devoir du tatami manager de s'assurer, avant chaque combat ou rencontre que les athlètes portent l'équipement approuvé.", "es": "Es obligación del tatami manager asegurarse antes de cada combate o encuentro de que los atletas llevan el equipamiento homologado.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.10 (Match Supervisor/KANSA, not Tatami Manager)"}, {"num": 191, "en": "WAZA -ARI is awarded for CHUDAN kicks.", "fr": "WAZA -ARI est accordé pour les coups de pied CHUDAN.", "es": "Se concederá WAZA -ARI por las patadas CHUDAN.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.6"}, {"num": 192, "en": "IPPON is awarded for JODAN kicks and any technique which is delivered on an opponent who has been thrown, has fallen on their own accord, or is otherwise off their feet.", "fr": "IPPON est accordé pour JODAN kicks et n'importe quelle technique qui sont délivrées sur un adversaire qui a été projeté, qui est tombé de son propre chef, ou qui est autrement que sur ses pieds.", "es": "IPPON se concede por JODAN patadas y qualquier técnica realizada sobre un oponente que ha sido derribado, ha caído por su propia falta, o se ha caido de cualquier forma.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.6 (omits HIZA GAMAE exception)"}, {"num": 193, "en": "Individual bouts cannot be declared a tie.", "fr": "Les combats individuels ne peuvent pas être déclarés nuls.", "es": "Los combates individuales no pueden ser declarados empate.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.5 (only individual ELIMINATION bouts; Round-robin can tie)"}, {"num": 194, "en": "Passivity can be given to any Athlete at any time.", "fr": "La passivité peut être accordée à n'importe quel athlète à n'importe quel moment.", "es": "Se puede dar pasividad a cualquier atleta en cualquier momento.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.1(10) / 10.4.15"}, {"num": 195, "en": "Passivity cannot be given during the first 15 seconds of a bout.", "fr": "La passivité ne peut être accordée pendant les 15 premières secondes d'un combat.", "es": "No se puede dar pasividad durante los primeros 15 segundos de un combate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.15 / 9.1.1(10)"}, {"num": 196, "en": "Simulated attacks with the head, knees, or elbows are offenses.", "fr": "Les attaques simulées avec la tête, les genoux ou les coudes sont des infractions.", "es": "Los ataques simulados con la cabeza, las rodillas o los codos son infracciones.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.1(15)"}, {"num": 197, "en": "Avoiding combat during the last 15 seconds of the bout (ATO SHIBARAKU) will as a minimum result in HANSOKU CHUI and loss of SENSHU.", "fr": "L'évitement du combat pendant les 15 dernières secondes du combat (ATO SHIBARAKU) entraînera au minimum HANSOKU CHUI et la perte de SENSHU.", "es": "Evitar el combate durante los últimos 15 segundos del combate (ATO SHIBARAKU) resultará como mínimo en HANSOKU CHUI y pérdida de SENSHU.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.16"}, {"num": 198, "en": "The Head Coach of a delegation can protest about a judgment to the members of the Referee Panel.", "fr": "L'entraîneur principal d'une délégation peut protester contre un jugement auprès les membres du panel d'arbitres.", "es": "El entrenador jefe de una delegación puede protestar sobre un juicio ante los miembros del panel de arbitraje.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 13.1.1"}, {"num": 199, "en": "Jacket ties must be tied.", "fr": "Les ficelles des vestes doivent être attachées.", "es": "Los lazos de las chaquetas deben estar atados.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(g)"}, {"num": 200, "en": "At the beginning of a bout jackets without ties can be used.", "fr": "Au début d'un combat, les vestes sans ficelles peuvent être utilisées.", "es": "Al comienzo de un combate se pueden utilizar chaquetas sin lazos.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(g)"}, {"num": 201, "en": "In individual competition, an Athlete can be replaced by another after the draw has taken place.", "fr": "En compétition individuelle, un athlète peut être remplacé par un autre après le tirage au sort.", "es": "En una competición individual, un atleta puede ser sustituido por otro después de haberse realizado el sorteo.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "No provision for individual-athlete replacement (contrast Art. 3.5 team back-ups)"}, {"num": 202, "en": "At medal bouts, male Coaches are required to wear a dark suit, shirt, tie and shoes covering the toes.", "fr": "Lors des combats pour les médailles, les coachs masculins doivent porter un costume sombre, une chemise, une cravate et des chaussures fermées couvrant les orteils.", "es": "En los combates por medallas los entrenadores masculinos deben llevar traje oscuro, camisa y corbata, además de zapatos que cubran todo el pie.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.3.1"}, {"num": 203, "en": "At medal bouts, female Coaches can choose to wear a dress, pantsuit or a combination of jacket and skirt in dark colours and shoes covering the toes.", "fr": "Lors des combats pour les médailles, les coaches féminines peuvent choisir de porter une robe, un tailleur -pantalon ou une combinaison veste -jupe de couleur sombre, avec des chaussures fermées couvrant les orteils.", "es": "En los combates por medallas, las entrenadoras podrán elegir entre llevar vestido, traje pantalón o una combinación de chaqueta y falda en colores oscuros, además de zapatos que cubran todo el pie.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.3.1"}, {"num": 204, "en": "At medal bouts, female Coaches cannot wear religious headwear.", "fr": "Lors des combats pour les médailles, les entraîneurs féminins ne peuvent pas porter de couvre -chef religieux.", "es": "En los combates por medallas, las entrenadoras no pueden llevar tocados religiosos.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.3.2(b)"}, {"num": 205, "en": "An Athlete that refuses to follow the instructions of the Referee or displays a loss of temper will automatically receive HANSOKU.", "fr": "Un athlète qui refuse de suivre les instructions de l'arbitre ou qui montre une perte de sang -froid recevra automatiquement un HANSOKU.", "es": "Un atleta que se niegue a seguir las instrucciones del árbitro o muestre una pérdida de temperamento recibirá automáticamente HANSOKU.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.17 (SHIKKAKU, not HANSOKU)"}, {"num": 206, "en": "Athletes are not entitled to a period of time between bouts, equal to the standard duration time of the bout, for purpose of rest.", "fr": "Les athlètes n'ont pas droit à une période de temps entre les combats, égale à la durée standard du combat, pour se reposer.", "es": "Los atletas no tienen derecho a un período de tiempo entre combates igual al tiempo de duración estándar del combate, con el propósito de descansar.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 5.5"}, {"num": 207, "en": "Passivity cannot be given after less than 15 seconds of bout time remaining.", "fr": "Passivité ne peut être infligée lorsqu’il reste moins de 15 secondes au combat.", "es": "La pasividad no puede darse cuando quedan menos de 15 segundos del combate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.1(10) / 10.4.15"}, {"num": 208, "en": "Any excessive celebration, such as falling on one's knees etc., political, or religious expressions, during or immediately after the bout or match, are prohibited and can be subject to a fine equal to the protest fee determined by the Executive Committee.", "fr": "Toute célébration excessive, telle que tomber à genoux, etc., toute expression politique ou religieuse, pendant ou immédiatement après le combat ou la rencontre, sont interdites et peuvent faire l'objet d'une amende égale à la taxe de protestation détermin ée par le comité exécutif.", "es": "Cualquier celebración excesiva, como arrodillarse, etc., expresiones políticas o religiosas, durante o inmediatamente después del combate, están prohibidas y pueden estar sujetas a una multa igual a la tasa de protesta determinada por la Comisión Ejecutiva .", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.5"}, {"num": 209, "en": "If an Athlete receives KIKEN, or SHIKKAKU, in Round -robin competition all previous bouts are voided from the result.", "fr": "Si un athlète reçoit un KIKEN ou un SHIKKAKU dans une compétition round - robin tous les combats précédents sont annulés.", "es": "Si un atleta recibe KIKEN, o SHIKKAKU, en competición round -robin, todos los combates anteriores serán anulados del resultado.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.7.2 (unless it's the last scheduled bout)"}, {"num": 210, "en": "Grabbing the opponent's arm or Karate Gi with one hand is only allowed for attempting an immediate scoring technique or takedown.", "fr": "Saisir le bras ou le Karate Gi de l'adversaire d'une seule main n'est autorisé que pour tenter une technique de point ou une projection immédiate.", "es": "Agarrar el brazo o Karate Gi del oponente con una mano, sólo está permitido para intentar una técnica inmediatamente puntuable o un derribo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.11"}, {"num": 211, "en": "Grabbing the opponent with both hands is never allowed during the bout.", "fr": "Il est toujours interdit de saisir l'adversaire à deux mains pendant le combat.", "es": "Agarrar al oponente con ambas manos nunca está permitido durante el combate.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.9 (allowed when catching a kicking leg)"}, {"num": 212, "en": "It is the Tatami Manager's duty to appoint the video review Judge.", "fr": "Il incombe au tatami manager de désigner le juge chargé de révision vidéo.", "es": "Es deber del tatami manager designar al juez de la revisión de vídeo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.2.1(5)"}, {"num": 213, "en": "If the number of IPPON and WAZA ARI is equal, the decision will be made by HANTEI.", "fr": "Si le nombre d'IPPON et de WAZA ARI est égal, la décision sera prise par HANTEI.", "es": "Si el número de IPPON y WAZA ARI es igual, la decisión será por HANTEI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.4"}, {"num": 214, "en": "In any individual bout, with equal score, and no SENSHU by either Athlete, the first criterion of the decision will be made based on the higher number of IPPON scored in the bout.", "fr": "Dans n'importe quel combat individuel, avec un score égal, et sans SENSHU pour l'un des athlètes, le premier critère de la décision sera basé sur le plus grand nombre d'IPPON obtenu dans le combat.", "es": "En cualquier combate individual, con igual puntuación y sin SENSHU por parte de ninguno de los atletas, el primer criterio de la decisión se tomará en base al mayor número de IPPON marcados en el combate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.3(a)"}, {"num": 215, "en": "If one Athlete has a score indicated by more than one Judge and the score is different between the Judges, the higher will be applied, unless there is majority for a lower score.", "fr": "Si un athlète obtient une note attribuée par plusieurs juges et que les notes attribuées par les juges diffèrent, la note la plus élevée sera retenue, sauf si une majorité se prononce en faveur d'une note inférieure.", "es": "Si un atleta tiene una puntuación indicada por más de un juez y la puntuación es diferente entre los jueces, se aplicará la más alta, a menos que haya una mayoría a favor de una puntuación más baja.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.1.3 / 12.1.4"}, {"num": 216, "en": "The Tatami Manager must notify the central table if an Athlete has been stopped from further competition based on the 10 -second rule.", "fr": "Le tatami manager doit informer la table centrale si un athlète a été exclu de la suite de la compétition en vertu de la règle des 10 secondes.", "es": "El tatami manager debe notificar a la mesa central si un atleta no puede seguir compitiendo, basándose en la regla de los 10 segundos.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.2.4"}, {"num": 217, "en": "The Timekeeper is responsible for starting the 3 -minute count for an Athlete who is injured during a bout in progress and requires medical treatment.", "fr": "Le chronométreur est responsable du démarrage du décompte des 3 minutes pour un athlète qui est blessé pendant un combat en cours et qui a besoin d'un traitement médical.", "es": "El anotador de puntuación es responsable de iniciar el recuento de 3 minutos para un atleta que se lesione durante un combate en curso y requiera tratamiento médico.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.2.3 (Tatami Manager is responsible, instructs the timekeeper)"}, {"num": 218, "en": "The Referee will not call YAME if an Athlete seizes the opponent and does not perform an immediate technique or throw.", "fr": "L'arbitre ne déclarera pas YAME si un athlète saisit son adversaire sans effectuer immédiatement une technique ou une projection.", "es": "El árbitro no anunciará YAME si un atleta agarra al oponente y no realiza una técnica o un lanzamiento inmediato.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.10(e)"}, {"num": 219, "en": "The Referee indicates the winner by hand signal and the order (AKA/AO NO KACHI), and by this action also resolves any tie.", "fr": "L'arbitre indiquera le vainqueur par un signe de la main et l'ordre AKA/AO NO KACHI, et par cette action, il résoudra également toute égalité.", "es": "El árbitro indicará el ganador mediante una señal con la mano y la orden (AKA/AO NO KACHI), y mediante esta acción también resolverá cualquier empate.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.7"}, {"num": 220, "en": "If an Athlete seizes the opponent, the Referee will give several seconds for the Athlete to perform a throw or technique.", "fr": "Si un athlète saisit son adversaire, l'arbitre donnera quelques secondes au athlète pour exécuter une projection ou une technique.", "es": "si un atleta agarra al oponente, el árbitro dará varios segundos para que el atleta realice un derribo o técnica.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.10(e) (YAME is called, no extended grace period)"}, {"num": 221, "en": "The Coach or NF representative will request the official protest form from the Tatami Manager.", "fr": "L'entraîneur ou le représentant de la FN demandera le formulaire officiel de protestation officielle au tatami manager.", "es": "El entrenador o representante de la FN solicitará la protesta oficial al tatami manager.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 13.1.6"}, {"num": 222, "en": "The Referee can stop the bout and give a point without the Judges' opinion.", "fr": "L'arbitre peut arrêter le combat et donner un point sans l'avis des juges.", "es": "El árbitro puede parar el combate y dar un punto sin la opinión de los jueces.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 8.1 (needs 2+ judges, or VR judge)"}, {"num": 223, "en": "If the Referee does not call the Doctor in a 10-second rule situation, KANSA must blow the whistle.", "fr": "Si l'arbitre n'appelle pas le médecin dans une situation de règle des 10 secondes, KANSA doit donner un coup de sifflet.", "es": "Si el árbitro no llama al médico en una situación de regla de 10 segundos, KANSA debe hacer sonar el silbato.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.4(15)"}, {"num": 224, "en": "The winning team is the one with the most bout victories excluding those won by SENSHU.", "fr": "L'équipe gagnante est celle qui a remporté le plus grand nombre de combats, à l'exception de ceux remportés par SENSHU.", "es": "El equipo ganador es el que tenga más combates ganados excluyendo los ganados por SENSHU.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.5.1 (including SENSHU wins)"}, {"num": 225, "en": "The red and blue belts must be no longer than three -quarters thigh length.", "fr": "Les ceintures rouges et bleues ne doivent pas être plus longues que les trois quarts de la longueur de la cuisse.", "es": "Los cinturones rojo y azul no deben ser más largos que tres cuartos de la longitud del muslo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 2.2.1(d)"}, {"num": 226, "en": "The correct penalty for feigning an injury if the Judges have determined that the technique in fact was a score, is HANSOKU.", "fr": "La pénalité correcte pour feindre une blessure si les juges ont déterminé que la technique était en fait un point, est HANSOKU.", "es": "La penalización correcta por fingir una lesión si los jueces han determinado que la técnica de hecho era una puntuación, es HANSOKU.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 10.4.5 (HANSOKU CHUI minimum, not straight HANSOKU)"}, {"num": 227, "en": "The information of officials implicated in the protest is completed by the Tatami Manager.", "fr": "L'information des officiels impliqués dans la protestation est complétée par le tatami manager.", "es": "La información de los oficiales implicados en la protesta es completada por el tatami manager.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 13.1.11"}, {"num": 228, "en": "Disqualification by KIKEN means that the Athlete is disqualified from that category, although it does not affect participation in another category.", "fr": "La disqualification par KIKEN signifie que les athlètes sont disqualifiés de cette catégorie, bien que cela n'affecte pas la participation dans une autre catégorie.", "es": "La descalificación por KIKEN significa que los atletas son descalificados de esa categoría, aunque no afecta a la participación en otra categoría.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 6.4"}, {"num": 229, "en": "Athletes are entitled to a rest period of time between bouts, equal to the standard duration time of the bout. The exception is in the case of change of equipment color, where this time is extended to five minutes.", "fr": "Les athlètes ont droit à une période de repos entre les combats, égale à la durée standard du combat. L'exception est dans le cas d'un changement de couleur d'équipement, où ce temps est étendu à cinq minutes.", "es": "Los atletas tienen derecho a un período de descanso entre combates igual al tiempo de duración estándar del combate. La excepción es en el caso de cambio de color de la equipacion donde este tiempo se amplía a cinco minutos.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 5.5"}, {"num": 230, "en": "In any bout, if after full time the scores are equal, but one Athlete has obtained SENSHU, that Athlete will be declared the winner.", "fr": "Dans n'importe quel combat, si après le temps complet les scores sont égaux, mais qu'un athlète a obtenu SENSHU, ce athlète sera déclaré vainqueur.", "es": "En cualquier combate, si después del tiempo completo las puntuaciones están igualadas, pero uno de los atletas ha obtenido SENSHU, ese atleta será declarado vencedor.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.1"}, {"num": 231, "en": "By SENSHU is understood that one Athlete has achieved the first instance of scoring on the opponent without having the opponent also score before the signal.", "fr": "Par SENSHU on entend qu'un athlète a réussi à marquer pour la première fois sur son adversaire sans que ce dernier ne marque également avant le signal.", "es": "Con SENSHU se entiende que un atleta ha conseguido la primera instancia de puntuación sobre el oponente sin que el oponente también haya puntuado antes de la señal.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.2"}, {"num": 232, "en": "In the event that an Athlete falls, is thrown, or knocked down and does not regain his or her feet immediately, the Referee will call the Doctor, and at the same time start a count to ten indicating his count showing a finger for each second.", "fr": "Dans le cas où un athlète tombe, est projeté ou renversé et ne se relève pas immédiatement, l'arbitre appellera le médecin et commencera en même temps à compter jusqu'à dix en montrant un doigt pour chaque seconde.", "es": "En el caso de que un atleta caiga o sea derribado y no se recupere inmediatamente, el árbitro llamará al médico y al mismo tiempo iniciará una cuenta hasta diez indicando su cuenta mostrando un dedo por cada segundo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 11.2.4"}, {"num": 233, "en": "An audible signal will be given by the Timekeeper 15 seconds before the actual end of the bout and the Referee will announce \"ATO SHIBARAKU\".", "fr": "Un signal sonore sera donné par le chronométreur 15 secondes avant la fin effective du combat et l'arbitre annoncera \"ATO SHIBARAKU\".", "es": "El cronometrador dará una señal acústica 15 segundos antes del final real del combate y el árbitro anunciará \"ATO SHIBARAKU\".", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 5.4 / Appendix 1"}, {"num": 234, "en": "KANSA must remain silent if the Referee gives a warning or penalty for passivity during ATO SHIBARAKU.", "fr": "KANSA doit rester silencieux si l'arbitre donne un avertissement ou une pénalité pour passivité pendant l'ATO SHIBARAKU.", "es": "KANSA debe permanecer en silencio si el árbitro da una advertencia o penalización por pasividad durante ATO SHIBARAKU.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.5.4(9)"}, {"num": 235, "en": "In individual categories with elimination format, a bout can be declared a tie.", "fr": "Dans les catégories individuelles avec le format d'élimination, un combat peut être déclaré nul.", "es": "En las categorías individuales con formato de eliminación, un combate puede declararse empate.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 12.2.5"}, {"num": 236, "en": "For all competition formats the Coach will be allowed one video review card for the Athlete.", "fr": "Pour tous les formates de compétition, l'entraîneur aura droit à une carte de révision vidéo pour l'athlète.", "es": "Para todos los formatos de competición, se permitirá al entrenador una tarjeta de revisión de video para el atleta.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 14.1 / 14.18 (varies by phase; not all formats use VR)"}, {"num": 237, "en": "The Athlete can ask the Coach to request a video review discreetely.", "fr": "L’athlète peut demander discrètement à l'entraîneur de demander une révision vidéo.", "es": "El atleta podrá pedir discretamente al entrenador que solicite una revisión de vídeo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 9.1.7"}, {"num": 238, "en": "The last six seconds before the bout was stopped for the request will always be evaluated for video review.", "fr": "Les six dernières secondes avant l'arrêt du combat pour la demande seront toujours évaluées pour la révision vidéo.", "es": "Los últimos six segundos antes de que el combate se detuviera para la solicitud serán siempre evaluados para la revisión por Video.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 14.8"}, {"num": 239, "en": "If both Coaches request video review at the same time, the video review Judge can only award the point to whoever is deemed to score first.", "fr": "Si les deux entraîneurs demandent une révision vidéo en même temps, le juge vidéo ne peut attribuer le point qu'à celui qui est considéré comme ayant marqué en premier.", "es": "Si ambos entrenadores solicitan la revisión del vídeo al mismo tiempo, el juez de vídeo solo podrá otorgar el punto a quien se considere que ha marcado primero.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 14.09 (exception for simultaneous scoring)"}, {"num": 240, "en": "Simultaneous scoring techniques can be awarded to both Athletes in video review.", "fr": "Les techniques simultanées peuvent être attribuées aux deux athlètes lors de la révision vidéo.", "es": "Las técnicas de puntuación simultánea pueden otorgarse a ambos atletas en la revisión por vídeo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 14.09"}, {"num": 241, "en": "The video review Judge cannot overrule any decision made by the Judges, with the exception of SENSHU.", "fr": "Le juge de la révision vidéo ne peut pas infirmer une décision des juges, à l'exception de SENSHU.", "es": "El juez de revisión de vídeo no podrá anular ninguna decisión de los jueces, con la excepción de SENSHU.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 14.12"}, {"num": 242, "en": "The Tatami Manager must supervise that KANSA stops the bout to instruct the Referee regarding a contravention of the Rules of Competition.", "fr": "Le tatami manager doit s'assurer que KANSA arrête le combat pour donner des instructions à l'arbitre concernant une infraction au règlement de compétition.", "es": "El tatami manager debe supervisar que KANSA detenga el combate para instruir al árbitro sobre una contravención del reglamento de competición.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.2.1(3)"}, {"num": 243, "en": "The Referee indicates fouls observed, and imposes warnings and penalties as required by the Rules.", "fr": "L'arbitre indique les fautes observées et impose les avertissements et les pénalités prévus par le règlement.", "es": "El árbitro indica las faltas observadas, e impone las advertencias y penalizaciones requeridas por el reglamento.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.3.1(7)"}, {"num": 244, "en": "Referee breaks the tie in case of HANTEI.", "fr": "L'arbitre rompt l'égalité en cas de HANTEI.", "es": "El árbitro deshace el empate en caso de HANTEI.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Art. 7.9"}, {"num": 245, "en": "In the event that the Referee does not hear the time-up bell, KANSA will blow his whistle.", "fr": "Si l'arbitre n'entend pas la sonnerie de fin de combat, KANSA sifflera.", "es": "En el caso de que el árbitro no oiga la señal de final de tiempo, KANSA hará sonar su silbato.", "answer": "FALSE", "rule_ref": "Art. 15.6.2 (Score-Supervisor, not KANSA)"}, {"num": 246, "en": "In the Two Judges System, the Judges will assist the Referee by giving signals for JOGAI and excessive contact.", "fr": "Dans le système à deux juges, les juges assisteront l'arbitre en donnant des signaux pour le JOGAI et le contact excessif.", "es": "En el sistema de dos jueces, los jueces asistirán al árbitro dando señales de JOGAI y contacto excesivo.", "answer": "TRUE", "rule_ref": "Appendix 5, item 2"}];
const ARTICLES = [{"article_no": "1", "title": "KUMITE COMPETITION AREA", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "2", "title": "ATTIRE AND PROTECTIVE EQUIPMENT", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "3", "title": "ORGANISATION OF KUMITE COMPETITIONS", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "4", "title": "THE REFEREE PANEL", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "5", "title": "DURATION OF BOUT", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "6", "title": "KIKEN – FAILURE TO APPEAR AT THE TATAMI", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "7", "title": "STARTING, SUSPENDING AND ENDING OF MATCHES", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "8", "title": "SCORING", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "9", "title": "PROHIBITED BEHAVIOUR", "page": 24}, {"article_no": "10", "title": "WARNINGS & PENALTIES", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "11", "title": "INJURIES AND ACCIDENTS IN COMPETITION", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "12", "title": "CRITERIA FOR DECISION", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "13", "title": "OFFICIAL PROTEST", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "14", "title": "VIDEO REVIEW REQUEST", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "15", "title": "POWERS AND DUTIES OF OFFICIALS", "page": 42}, {"article_no": "16", "title": "ELIGIBILITY TO COMPETE", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "17", "title": "ADAPTATION OF THESE RULES TO EVENTS OUTSIDE THE WKF OFFICIAL EVENT PROGRAMME", "page": 47}, {"article_no": "18", "title": "ISSUES NOT SPECIFICALLY COVERED BY THE RULES", "page": 48}, {"article_no": "App1", "title": "THE TERMINOLOGY", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App2", "title": "GESTURES AND FLAG SIGNALS", "page": 50}, {"article_no": "App3", "title": "CATEGORIES, AGE & WEIGHT DIVISIONS", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App4", "title": "OFFICIAL PROTEST FORM", "page": 56}, {"article_no": "App5", "title": "TWO JUDGE SYSTEM", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App6", "title": "SUMMARY TABLE OF WINNING CRITERIA AND TIE RESOLUTION", "page": 59}];
const SECTIONS = [{"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.1", "text": "The competition area will be a WKF Approved matted square, with sides of eight metres (measured from the outside) with the mats in the outer one-metre area in another colour, marking the boundary. There will be a 2 metres safety area surrounding the competition area.", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.2", "text": "There will be a minimum of 2 metres between competition areas.", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.3", "text": "There must be no advertisements, signs, walls, pillars, etc. within one metre of the safety area's outer perimeter.", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.4", "text": "Where monitors or displays are placed between the competition areas, these must be placed far enough from the competition areas to allow a safety area of 2 metres between competition areas on all sides. (The monitors must be placed at a minimum of 2 metres from the outside of the outer different coloured warning area.)", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.5", "text": "Two mats are inverted with the red (or otherwise coloured) side turned up in one metre distance from the mat centre to form a boundary between the Athletes. When starting or resuming combat, the Athletes will be standing front and centre on the mat facing each other.", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.6", "text": "The Referee (SHUSHIN) will be standing centred between the two mats, facing the Athletes at a distance of two metres from the boundary of the competition area. Each Judge (FUKUSHIN) will be seated at the designated area. If seated on the TATAMI, they will be placed approximately 1.5 metres off the corners in the safety area.", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.7", "text": "The Referee may move around the entire Tatami, including the safety area where the Judges are seated. Each Judge will be equipped with a red and a blue flag or an electronic signal device.", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.8", "text": "The Match Supervisor (KANSA) will be seated at the official table. They will be equipped with a whistle.", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.9", "text": "The Score Supervisor will be seated at the official score table beside the score/timekeeper, and where video is deployed, so will the Video Review Judge.", "page": 3}, {"article_no": "1", "section_no": "1.10", "text": "Coaches will be seated outside the safety area, on their respective sides of the TATAMI towards the official table. In cases where the configuration of Tatami makes it impractical to place the Coaches facing the official table, they may instead be placed on each side of the official table. If in such cases, video review is used, Coach supervisors must be deployed. Rules Version 2026.01 4 Flag System Competition Set Up Initial Rounds Medal bouts Joysticks System Competition Set Up Initial Rounds Medal bouts Rules Version 2026.01 5", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.1", "text": "Referees and Judges", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.1.1", "text": "The official uniform will be as follows: a) A single-breasted navy-blue blazer (colour code 19-4023 TPX) b) Plain light-grey trousers without turn-ups (colour code 18-0201 TPX) c) A white shirt with short sleeves d) Plain dark blue or black socks and black slip-on shoes for use on the match area e) An official tie, worn without a tiepin f) A black whistle with a discreet white cord for the whistle", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.1.2", "text": "The following additions to attire are allowed: a) A plain wedding band b) Voluntary religious headwear approved by the WKF c) A hairclip and discreet earrings d) Hair must be worn off the shoulders and make-up must be discreet e) Heels of more than 4 cm may not be worn with the uniform It is strictly forbidden for officials to use phones, wear smartwatches, or make use of private electronic devices within the confines of the field of play. Sunglasses are not allowed.", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.1.3", "text": "Referees and Judges must wear the official uniform at all tournaments, seminars, briefings, and courses.", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.1.4", "text": "For multisport events where a cross-sport uniform is provided for Referees at the cost of the LOC with the feel and look of the specific event, the official uniform for Referees might be substituted by that common uniform, provided that it is requested in writing to the WKF by the event organiser and formally approved by the WKF.", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.1.5", "text": "If the Chief Referee agrees, refereeing officials may be allowed to remove their blazers.", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.1.6", "text": "The Referee Commission or Chief Referee may refuse the participation of any official who does not comply with these rules.", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2", "text": "Athletes", "page": 5}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.1", "text": "Athletes must wear a WKF Approved white Karategi without piping or personal embroidery other than allowed explicitly by the WKF EC and specified in the bulletin for the competition: a) For all official WKF events (World Championships and Karate 1 - Premier League, Series A and Youth League), the Karategi must have embroidered brands on the shoulders in red or blue, respectively, according to the draw. Exceptions include the grand winners of the previous Premier League season, who should wear a gold shoulder embroidery in current Premier League events, and the incumbent Senior World Champion, who should wear a gold shoulder embroidery in the current Senior World Championship. This applies equally to individuals and teams. There is no WKF requirement for the Team members wearing the same brand of Karategi. b) Only the original manufacturer’s labels may be displayed on the Karategi. Rules Version 2026.01 6 The national emblem or flag of the country will be worn on the left breast of the jacket and may not exceed an overall size of 12cm by 8cm. In addition, identification issued by the Organising Committee will be worn on the back. The back number is mandatory for Karate 1 – Premier League, Karate World Championships and Karate World Cup. Rules Version 2026.01 7 c) Athletes or Teams must wear a WKF Approved red belt (AKA) or blue belt (AO) as allocated by the draw, without any personal embroideries, advertising or markings other than the customary label from the manufacturer. Belts of grade cannot be worn during the bout. d) The red and blue belts must be around five centimetres wide and of a length sufficient to allow fifteen centimetres free on each side of the knot, but not longer than three- quarters of thigh length. e) The jacket, when tightened around the waist with the belt, must be of a minimum length that covers the hips, but must not be more than three-quarters of thigh length. f) Female Athletes can wear a plain white T-shirt beneath the Karate jacket. g) Jackets without ties cannot be used. The jacket ties holding the jacket in place must be tied at the beginning of the bout. If they are torn off during the bout, the Athlete is not required to change the jacket. h) The maximum length of the jacket sleeves must be no longer than the bend of the wrist and no shorter than halfway down the forearm. i) Jacket sleeves cannot be rolled up. j) The trousers must be long enough to cover at least two-thirds of the shin and must not reach below the anklebone. Trouser legs cannot be rolled up. k) The Karategi must not be altered or manipulated to change its shape.", "page": 7}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.2", "text": "The WKF Executive Committee can authorise the display of special labels or trademarks (brand logos) of approved sponsors.", "page": 7}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.3", "text": "Athletes must keep their hair clean and cut to a length that does not obstruct smooth bout conduct. Hachimaki (headband) will not be allowed.", "page": 7}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.4", "text": "Hair slides are prohibited, as are metal hairgrips. Ribbons, beads and other decorations are prohibited. One or two discreet rubber bands on a single ponytail are permitted.", "page": 7}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.5", "text": "Athletes may, according to their own individual choice, use religious headwear approved by the WKF: A black plain fabric head scarf covering the hair, but not the neck or throat area.", "page": 7}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.6", "text": "Athletes must have short fingernails and must not wear metallic or other objects, which might injure their opponents. The use of metallic teeth braces must be approved by the Referee and the Tournament Doctor. The Athlete accepts full responsibility for any injury.", "page": 7}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.7", "text": "The following protective equipment is compulsory: a) WKF Approved mitts, one Athlete wearing red and the other wearing blue. b) Gum shield. c) WKF Approved body protector for males. Females are to use a chest and body protector or the integrated chest/body protector. d) WKF Approved shin pads, one Athlete wearing red and the other wearing blue. e) WKF Approved foot protection, one Athlete wearing red and the other wearing blue. f) WKF Approved groin guards for male Athletes. g) For Athletes under 14 years of age, the use of a WKF Approved helmet and external body protector is compulsory. h) For Female Athletes under 14 years of age, the use of WKF Approved chest protector is also compulsory.", "page": 7}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.8", "text": "Glasses are forbidden. Soft contact lenses can be worn at the Athlete's own risk.", "page": 7}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.9", "text": "The wearing of any unauthorised apparel, clothing or equipment is forbidden. Rules Version 2026.01 8", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.10", "text": "It is the duty of the Match Supervisor to ensure, before each match or bout, that the Athletes are wearing the approved equipment. All protective equipment must be WKF Approved.", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.11", "text": "In the case of Continental Federations, they will limit themselves to providers and brands already approved for WKF. National Federations must also accept all WKF Approved equipment for all local, regional or national competitions.", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.12", "text": "The use of bandages, padding, or supports because of injury must be approved by the Referee and done or approved by the Tournament Doctor.", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.13", "text": "In case that deformities or amputations that do not allow for safe and secure fitting of the protective equipment or could represent a risk to the athlete or their opponents, competitive Kumite will not be permitted. In any doubt, the Referees should ask the doctor for the decision.", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.2.14", "text": "Athletes that appear at the competition area with unauthorized equipment or irregular Karategi will be given two minutes to correct the attire, and the Coach based on the report from the Chief Referee may have their coaching license suspended for a period of up to 6 months starting the date after the applicable tournament unless the equipment and attire has been checked beforehand by a WKF Controller.", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.3", "text": "Coaches", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.3.1", "text": "Coaches must at all times during the tournament, briefing, and courses wear the official tracksuit of their National Federation, wear shoes, and display their official identification. The exception is bouts/matches for medals in official WKF events, where male Coaches are required to wear a dark suit, shoes covering the feet, shirt and tie. Female Coaches may choose to wear a dress, pantsuit, or a combination of jacket and skirt in dark colours and shoes. Sandals, or any other open-toe shoes, are prohibited. Sunglasses are not allowed.", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.3.2", "text": "In addition, the following additions to attire are allowed: a) A plain wedding band. b) Religious headwear approved by the WKF.", "page": 8}, {"article_no": "2", "section_no": "2.3.3", "text": "The Chief Referee can allow Coaches to use the federation’s official Team t-shirt or a plain coloured t-shirt without writing or logos instead of the tracksuit jacket. Rules Version 2026.01 9", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.1", "text": "Definitions", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.1.1", "text": "A “bout” refers to an individual bout between two Athletes.", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.1.2", "text": "A “match” is the total of all bouts between the members of two Teams.", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.1.3", "text": "The term “group” is here used about the Athletes participating in one of the eight or more groups in the Round-robin phase for individual competition or the group of five Teams participating in round-robin Team competition.", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.1.4", "text": "The term “pool” is used for each of the two halves of the total number of Athletes in a category, forming the two paths of advancement towards competing for the medals.", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.1.5", "text": "A “runner-up” refers to the second place Athlete in a Round-robin group.", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.2", "text": "Weigh-in procedure", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.2.1", "text": "Rehearsal weighing Athletes shall be allowed to check their weight on the official weigh-in scales (that will be used for the official weigh-in) from one hour before the official weigh-in commences. There is no limit to the number of times each Athlete may check their weight during the time of the unofficial weigh-in.", "page": 9}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.2.2", "text": "Official weighing: a) Place: The weight control will always take place in only one location. The possibilities to host this control are the competition venue, the official hotel or the village (To be announced for each event). Organizers must provide separate rooms for men and women. b) Scales: If the official scale shows a higher weight than the scale provided for test weighing, the Athlete can demand to be weighed again, applying the weight shown on the test scale as the official result of the weigh-in. The host NF should provide enough calibrated electronic scales (at least 4 units) showing only one decimal place, e.g. 51.9 kg, 104.6 kg. The scale should be placed on a solid floor that is not carpeted. c) Time: Weigh-in must take place no later than the day before the competition for the category, unless specified otherwise for a specific competition. The official weigh-in time for WKF events will be duly announced on the bulletin. For any other events, this information will be distributed in advance through the OC communication channels. It is the responsibility of the Athlete to be aware of this information. An Athlete who does not turn up for the weigh-in period or fails to weigh within the prescribed limits for the category in which the Athlete is registered will be disqualified (KIKEN). Rules Version 2026.01 1 d) Tolerance: The tolerances admitted are 0.2 kg for all male categories and 0.5 kg for all female categories. The same tolerance applies to both the upper and lower limits of a weight class. e) Procedure: A minimum of two WKF officials are required at the weigh-in for each gender. One to check the accreditation/passport of the Athlete, and one to record the exact weight on the official weigh-in list. An additional six staff members (officials/volunteers) supplied by the host NF should also be available to control the flow of Athletes. Twelve chairs must be supplied. To protect the privacy of the Athletes, officials, as well as the staff members supervising the weigh-in, must be of the same gender as the Athletes. 1. The official weigh-in will be done category by category and Athlete by Athlete. 2. All Coaches and other Team delegates must leave the weigh-in room before the start of the official weigh-in. 3. The Athlete is allowed to stand on the scales only once during the official weigh- in period. 4. Each Athlete shall bring to the weigh-in their accreditation card issued for the event and shall present it to the official, who will verify the identity of the Athlete. 5. The official then invites the Athlete to stand on the scales. 6. The Athlete shall weigh-in wearing only underclothing (men/boys – underpants, women/girls – underpants and bra). Any socks or additional complements must be removed. 7. The official supervising the weigh-in shall note and record the Athlete’s weight in kilograms (accurate to one decimal point of a kilogram). 8. The Athlete steps off the scales. NOTE: Photography or filming is not permitted in the weigh-in area. This includes the use of mobile phones and all other devices.", "page": 10}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.3", "text": "Seeding", "page": 10}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.3.1", "text": "For the Phase 2 of the WKF World Championships, the four highest ranked Athletes present at the competition are seeded by their respective ranking in the WKF World Ranking as per the day before the competition.", "page": 10}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.3.2", "text": "For World Cup competition, the medallist plus the loser of the bronze medal from the previous World Cup will be seeded.", "page": 10}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.3.3", "text": "For other WKF competitions, refer to the respective organising rules regarding seeding procedures.” Rules Version 2026.01 1", "page": 11}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.4", "text": "Competition formats", "page": 11}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.4.1", "text": "Karate Kumite competition takes the form of individual competition divided by gender, age groups, and weight categories or Team competition by gender without weight categories or mixed teams, either with or without weight categories, and can be organised in several formats: a) Elimination system with repechage for Individuals or Teams. (Used unless otherwise specified for the competition). b) Round-robin in groups followed by Elimination for individuals or Teams. (Used for individual Premier League competitions and the Senior World Championships for both individuals and Teams). c) Two-pool Round-robin system (used for multisport games).", "page": 11}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.4.2", "text": "The Elimination system with repechage will be applied unless otherwise pre-determined for a specific competition or series of tournaments.", "page": 11}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.4.3", "text": "For individual competition in Premier League, the Senior Individual World Championships and the World Team Championships, the Round-robin system followed by Elimination is applied.", "page": 11}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.4.4", "text": "For multisport games, such as continental games, Olympic Games, or other multisport events, the format of competition will be determined for each event depending on modalities included and restrictions on participation. The format used is normally a two-pool system where the winners of the pools go to the final.", "page": 11}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5", "text": "Composition of Kumite Teams", "page": 11}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5.1", "text": "Matches in Kumite for male Teams consist of 5 bouts. The Team must present 5 participants for the initial match. To participate in Round-robin competition, the Team must also have 2 additional back-up Athletes registered for possible participation in subsequent bouts and may also have a third optional back-up Athlete - bringing the maximum size of the Team to 8 Athletes. For any elimination matches, the Team must always have a minimum of 3 participants in order to compete.", "page": 11}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5.2", "text": "Matches in Kumite for female Teams consist of 3 bouts. The Team must present 3 participants for the initial match. To participate in Round-robin competition, the Team must also have 1 additional back-up Athlete registered for possible participation in subsequent bouts and may also have a second optional back-up Athlete - bringing the maximum size of the Team to 5 Athletes. For any elimination match, the Team must always have a minimum of 2 participants in order to compete. Rules Version 2026.01 1", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5.3", "text": "In Team Kumite competition without weight categories, the Team change which of the Team members should participate in each match. For a tie-break bout, the Team may submit a single name as they would normally do for a new round.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5.4", "text": "During Round-robin competition, the Team must complete all bouts in order to remain in the competition. If it does not, all bouts and matches will be voided, and no victory points or scoring points will be counted. Likewise, all victory points and scoring points earned by other Teams in meeting the Team eliminated will be voided.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5.5", "text": "In the second match of an Elimination tournament, and in the Elimination phase following Round-robin, male Teams can never present fewer than 3 Athletes for a match and female Teams can never present fewer than 2.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5.6", "text": "Matches in Mixed Team Competition consist of 4 or 6 bouts, with an equal number of Athletes of each gender. The Team must present a full team for the initial round. For any subsequent rounds the team must present a number of Athletes sufficient to win by the number of bouts won.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5.7", "text": "In Mixed Team Competition by weight categories each team must present all Athletes in all designated weight categories, both male and female.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.5.8", "text": "The designated weight categories for Mixed Team Competition are those used for multiple sport games, 3 male and 3 female to a total of 6 weight categories.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6", "text": "Fighting order for Teams", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6.1", "text": "Before each match, a Team representative must hand to the official table an official form defining the names and fighting order of the competing Team members.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6.2", "text": "The fighting order form can be presented by the Coach or a nominated Athlete from the Team. If the Coach hands in the form, they must be clearly identifiable as such; otherwise, it can be rejected. The list must include the name of the country, the belt colour allocated to the Team for that match and the fighting order of the Team members. Both the Athletes’ names and their tournament numbers must be included, and the form must be signed by the Coach or a nominated person.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6.3", "text": "Coaches must present their accreditation together with that of their Athlete or Team to the Coach Supervisor or Kansa Assistant. For Team competition, it is allowed to use two Coaches, but only one Coach can actively be coaching in each bout, while the other must sit in the chair provided without interfering with the progress of the bout.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6.4", "text": "When lining up before a match, a Team will present the actual fighters for that round. The unused fighter(s) and the Coach will not be included and shall sit in an area set aside for them.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6.5", "text": "The participants can be selected for each round from the full Team. Their fighting order can be changed for each round, provided the new fighting order is notified before the round, but once notified, it cannot be changed until that round is completed.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6.6", "text": "The Team will be disqualified (SHIKKAKU) if any of its members or its Coach changes the Team's composition or fighting order without written notification prior to the round.", "page": 12}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6.7", "text": "If, through an error in charting, the wrong Athlete/Team competes, then regardless of the Rules Version 2026.01 1 outcome, that bout/match is declared null and void. To reduce such errors, the Score Supervisor must confirm the winning Athlete/Team with the software technician immediately after the bout/match.", "page": 13}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.6.8", "text": "In Team matches where an individual loses on account of receiving KIKEN, HANSOKU or SHIKKAKU, any score for the disqualified Athlete will be set to zero, and a score of 8-0 (counted as YUKO) will be recorded for that bout in favour of the other Team.", "page": 13}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.7", "text": "Round-robin, Individual Competition", "page": 13}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.7.1", "text": "In individual Premier League events, Round-robin competition using groups of 4 Athletes, the maximum 32 participants are divided into 8 groups of 4 Athletes or fewer. The winner of each of the eight groups go on to regular quarterfinals, semi-finals and final. The losers to the finalists in the quarter- and semi-finals compete for the bronze medals. While in Individual World Senior Championship Phase 2, the winners and runners-up of each of the 8 groups advance to the regular round 16, quarterfinals, semi-finals and final. The losers to the finalists in the quarter- and semi-finals compete for the bronze medals. Rules Version 2026.01 1", "page": 14}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.7.2", "text": "According to the number of Athletes (32 or less), the allocation to groups will be as per the following table: Number of Athletes/Groups Athletes per group Notes 8 Groups 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Participation: 24-32 Athletes Seed ► 3 2 4 1 32 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 The first of each Group qualify. 31 4 4 4 4 4 4 4 3 30 4 4 4 3 4 4 4 3 29 4 3 4 3 4 4 4 3 28 4 3 4 3 4 3 4 3 27 4 3 4 3 3 3 4 3 26 3 3 4 3 3 3 4 3 25 3 3 3 3 3 3 4 3 24 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 3 6 Groups 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Participation:18-23 Athletes Seed ► 3 2 4 1 23 4 4 4 4 4 3 The first of each Group and the two best runners-up qualify. 22 4 4 3 4 4 3 21 4 3 3 4 4 3 20 4 3 3 4 3 3 19 4 3 3 3 3 3 18 3 3 3 3 3 3 5 Groups 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Participation: 17 Athletes Seed ► 3 2 4 1 17 3 3 4 4 3 The first of each Group and the best three runners-up qualify. 4 Groups 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Participation: 12-16 Athletes Seed ► 3 2 4 1 16 4 4 4 4 The first and runner-up of each Group. 15 4 4 4 3 14 4 3 4 3 13 3 3 4 3 12 3 3 3 3 3 Groups 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Participation: 9-11 Athletes Seed ► 3 2 1 11 4 4 3 The first and runner-up of each Group, as well as the best two number- threes qualify. 10 4 3 3 9 3 3 3 2 Groups 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Participation: 6-8 Athletes Seed ► 2 1 8 4 4 The first and runner-up of each Group, will compete directly in the semi-finals. 7 4 3 6 3 3 1 Group 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 Participation: 3-5 Athletes Seed ► 1 5 5 Final between first and runner-up of the Group, and only one bronze medal bout. 4 4 3 3 Rules Version 2026.01 1", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.7.3", "text": "If an individual is disqualified or is unable to complete all bouts in the Round-robin, the scores of completed or current bouts will be nullified, and their victory points forfeited, unless it is the last bout of the Round-robin, in which case, all previous results and points remain unchanged.", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.7.4", "text": "The winner and runner-up of each group are determined by whoever has the most victory points by counting wins as three points per win, one point for a draw where points are scored. Bouts lost or draws with no scores give zero points.", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.7.5", "text": "The winners of the semi-finals will then go on to the final, where they compete for gold and silver.", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.7.6", "text": "Those who have lost to the finalists in the quarter finals and semi-finals will compete for the bronze medals (One for groups 1-4 and one for groups 5-8).", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.8", "text": "Phase 1 of the Individual World Championships For Phase 1 of the Individual World Championships, there is no limitation to 32 Athletes per category, and when required, the number of groups will be increased as well as the number of Athletes within the same group. Additional rounds of Round-robin will be fought until the number of winners qualified to proceed is 24 or less, after which straight Elimination bouts will determine the 6 winners that will qualify for Phase 2.", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.9", "text": "World Cup for National Teams For the World Cup, the Round-robin system followed by quarterfinals, semi-finals and final is applied. 5 Teams are allocated to each group. The winners and the runners-up of each group then compete in quarter-finals, semi-finals, and the final. After the Group Phase, the Group Winners and runners-up advance to the quarter-finals, where the bout winners head to the Semi-Finals and the winner to the Finals. Those who have lost to the finalists in the semi-finals will compete for one bronze medal. The winner of the finals receives the gold medal while the loser receives a silver medal. The winner of the bronze match will take bronze, while the losing Team is not awarded a medal.", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.10", "text": "Variations to competition formats If a variation of the competition format other than described in these rules is to be applied for a particular tournament, this must be clearly announced in the tournament bulletin.", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.11", "text": "Coaching", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.11.1", "text": "In World Championships, Kumite Coaches need to be part of a National Federation delegation and have the required Coach certification level when acting during the bout of an Athlete.", "page": 15}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.11.2", "text": "Exceptionally, in competitions with Video Review and upon prior request of the NF, WKF may authorize a Coach from a different delegation to act as a Coach for their delegation in the situations herein, provided that they comply with the dress code as established in art. 2.3.1, in order to cover the special circumstances arising from the need to have a Coach to request Video Review: Rules Version 2026.01 1 • A NF having registered one or more Coaches in Kumite categories, but the Coach(es) cannot attend the event due to visa problems, transport incidents, sudden health issues or any other justified cause, • A NF that, for budgetary reasons or being part of the WKF development programme, does not have funds to include Kumite Coach(es) within their delegation, • A Refugee athlete, or • A Coach being disqualified from competition, and as a result, the Athletes of their NF do not have any Kumite Coach.", "page": 16}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.11.3", "text": "If a NF is in any of the above-mentioned situations, and only during a World Championships, the OC Chair may authorize (subject to the President’s ratification) to make an exception.", "page": 16}, {"article_no": "3", "section_no": "3.11.4", "text": "In official WKF events, with the exception of Youth League, it is not permitted to change the Coach during a bout. In team matches, it is allowed to change the Coach between bouts. Rules Version 2026.01 1", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.1", "text": "Composition", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.1.1", "text": "The Refereeing Panel for each bout shall consist of one Referee (SHUSHIN), four Judges (FUKUSHIN), one Match Supervisor (KANSA), a Score Supervisor, and, where video review is used, a Video Review Judge.", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.1.2", "text": "The Referee, Judges, Match Supervisor, Score Supervisor, and Video Review Judge of a Kumite bout must not have the nationality or be from the same National Federation of either of the participants or have any other conflict of interest. It remains the duty of any official to self- report on any possible conflict of interest before the bout or match starts.", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.2", "text": "Referees and Judges’ deployment and panel allocation", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.2.1", "text": "For the eliminatory rounds, the RC Secretary will deliver to the software system technician handling the electronic drawing system a list containing the Referees and Judges available per TATAMI. This list is done by the RC Secretary once the Athletes’ draw is finished and at the end of the Referees’ Briefing. This list must only contain Referees present at the Briefing and must comply with the above-mentioned criteria. Then, for the Referees draw, the software technician will enter the list in the system, and 4 Judges, 1 Referee, 1 Match Supervisor (KANSA), and 1 Score Supervisor out of each TATAMI deployment will be randomly allocated as Referee Panel for each bout.", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.2.2", "text": "Where video review is used, a Video Review Judge is allocated in the same manner.", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.2.3", "text": "For medal bouts, the Tatami Managers will provide the RC Chairman and Secretary with a list containing 8 officials from their own TATAMI after the last bout of the eliminatory rounds is finished. Once the list is approved by the RC Chairman, it will be given to the software technician to be entered into the system. The system will then randomly allocate the Referee panel, which will only contain 5 out of the 8 officials from each TATAMI.", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.3", "text": "Supporting officials", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.3.1", "text": "In addition, for facilitating the operation of bouts/matches, 1 Tatami Manager, 3 Tatami Manager Assistants, and 1 Score/Timekeeper shall be appointed plus 2 Kansa Assistants for checking the Athlete’s equipment and 2 Coach Supervisors in instances where the configuration of TATAMI makes it necessary to see the Coaches requests for video review, or for any other reason deemed necessary by the Chief Referee.", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.3.2", "text": "Before the start of each match or bout, Kansa Assistants will ensure that Athletes’ equipment and Karategi are in accordance with the WKF rules of competition. In competitions where Kansa Assistant is not applicable or available, it is KANSA`s responsibility to ensure that the equipment is in accordance with the rules before each bout.", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.4", "text": "Formalities and change of judges", "page": 17}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.4.1", "text": "At the start of a Kumite match, the Referee stands on the outside edge of the match area. On the Referee’s left stand Judges numbers 1 and 2, and on the right stand Judges numbers 3 and 4. Rules Version 2026.01 1", "page": 18}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.4.2", "text": "After the formal exchange of bows by Athletes and the Referee panel, the Referee takes a step back, the Judges turn towards the Referee, and all bow together. All then take up their positions.", "page": 18}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.4.3", "text": "When changing the Judges, the departing Officials, except the Match Supervisor, line up, bow together (REI), and then leave the area.", "page": 18}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.4.4", "text": "When individual Judges change, the incoming Judge goes to the outgoing Judge, they bow together and change positions.", "page": 18}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.4.5", "text": "In Team matches, provided that the entire panel holds the required qualification, the positions of Referee and Judges must be rotated between each bout. If one or more officials do not hold the required qualification as Referee, they will remain as sitting Judges and be omitted from the rotation.", "page": 18}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.5", "text": "Procedure for refereeing Kumite with only two corner Judges", "page": 18}, {"article_no": "4", "section_no": "4.5.1", "text": "For Youth League competitions, the use of only two corner Judges is allowed. This procedure is described in APPENDIX 5. Rules Version 2026.01 1", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "5", "section_no": "5.1", "text": "Duration of the Kumite bout is: • Senior Male and Female categories: 3 minutes effective time • Under 21 Male and Female categories: 3 minutes effective time • Cadet and Junior Male and Female categories: 2 minutes effective time • Under 14 years", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "5", "section_no": "1.5", "text": "minutes effective time", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "5", "section_no": "5.2", "text": "For tournaments without limitation to participation, the duration of Elimination bouts may be reduced from 3 minutes to 2 minutes and from 2 minutes to 1.5 minutes, provided that this is announced prior to tournament start in a meeting for both Coaches and officials.", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "5", "section_no": "5.3", "text": "The timing of the bout starts when the Referee gives the signal to start and stops each time the Referee calls “YAME\", when two or more judges give the electronic signal for a score, or at the signal for full time.", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "5", "section_no": "5.4", "text": "The timekeeper shall give a signal, indicating “15 seconds to go” by one short burst with the buzzer, and “time up” by two short bursts with the buzzer. The “time up” signal marks the end of the bout.", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "5", "section_no": "5.5", "text": "Athletes are entitled to a rest period between bouts, equal to the standard duration time of the bout. The exception is in the case of a change of equipment colour, where this time is extended to five minutes.", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "6", "section_no": "6.1", "text": "KIKEN is the decision given when an Athlete or Athletes fail to present themselves when called, are unable to continue, abandon the bout, or are withdrawn on the order of the Tournament Doctor. The grounds for abandonment may include injury not ascribable to the opponent’s actions.", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "6", "section_no": "6.2", "text": "Individual Athletes or Teams that do not present themselves when called will be disqualified (KIKEN) from that category. In Team matches, the score for the bout not taking place will then be set to 8-0 (counted as YUKO) in favour of the other Team. In Individual Round-robin, the score for the bout will be set to 4-0 (counted as YUKO).", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "6", "section_no": "6.3", "text": "Points earned as a result of the opponent’s disqualification are always counted as YUKO.", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "6", "section_no": "6.4", "text": "Disqualification by KIKEN means that the Athletes are disqualified from that category, although it does not affect participation in another category.", "page": 19}, {"article_no": "6", "section_no": "6.5", "text": "When announcing disqualification by KIKEN, the Referee will signal by pointing their finger towards the side of the missing Athlete or Team, announcing “AKA/AO KIKEN”, and then “AKA/AO no KACHI”, giving the signal for KACHI (win) for the opponent. Rules Version 2026.01 1", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.1", "text": "The terms and gestures to be used by the Referee and Judges in the operation of a bout/match shall be as specified in APPENDIX 2.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.2", "text": "For each round, there will be a bowing ceremony starting with the Referee first having Athletes and officials face the audience and bow SHOMEN NI REI, followed by a bow to each other, OTAGAI NI REI. At the end of the bout(s), the bowing ceremony is done in the opposite sequence.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.3", "text": "The Referee and Judges shall take up their prescribed positions and, following an exchange of bows between the Athletes who are positioned at the front on their assigned mats nearest their opponent, the Referee will announce “SHOBU HAJIME!” and the bout will commence.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.4", "text": "The Athletes must bow properly to each other at the start and the end of the bout – a quick nod is both discourteous and insufficient.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.5", "text": "The Referee will stop the bout by announcing “YAME”. If necessary, the Referee will order the Athletes to take up their original positions: “MOTO NO ICHI” and return to their position.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.6", "text": "In the case of a score to be awarded, the Referee identifies the Athlete (AKA or AO), the area attacked (JODAN or CHUDAN), the technique (TSUKI, UCHI or KERI), and then awards the relevant score (YUKO, WAZA-ARI or IPPON) using the prescribed gesture. The Referee then restarts the bout by calling “TSUZUKETE HAJIME”.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.7", "text": "When an Athlete has been awarded a score that results in a lead of eight points or more, the bout is over. The winner is declared by the Referee raising a hand on the side of the winner and declaring “AO (AKA) NO KACHI”.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.8", "text": "When time is up, the Athlete who has the most points is declared the winner, indicated by the Referee raising a hand on the side of the winner, and declaring “AO (AKA) NO KACHI”. The bout has ended at this point.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.9", "text": "In the event of a tied score at the end of an inconclusive bout, the Referee Panel (the Referee and the four Judges) will decide the bout by HANTEI. The four judges will immediately give the signal after the Referee calls for “HANTEI” and blows the whistle. The Referee will thereafter raise their arm and declare the winner, “AO (AKA) NO KACHI”, and if necessary, by this action, break the tie.", "page": 20}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.10", "text": "When faced with the following situations, the Referee will call “YAME!” and halt the bout temporarily: a) When either or both Athletes are out of the Competition area, with the exception of allowing an Athlete to immediately score on an opponent who has exited the competition area. b) When the Referee orders the Athlete to adjust the KARATEGI or protective equipment. c) When an Athlete has contravened the rules. d) When the Referee considers that one or both of the Athletes cannot continue with the bout owing to injuries, illness or other causes, in accordance with the Tournament Doctor’s opinion, the Referee will decide whether the bout should be continued. Rules Version 2026.01 20 e) When an Athlete seizes the opponent and does not perform an immediate technique or throw. f) When one or both Athletes fall or are thrown, and neither Athlete manages to immediately follow up with a scoring technique. g) When both Athletes seize or clinch with each other without immediately succeeding in executing a throw or a scoring technique, or do not immediately respond to WAKARETE. h) When both Athletes stand chest to chest without immediately attempting a throw or other technique and do not respond to WAKARETE. i) When both Athletes are off their feet following a fall or attempted throw and begin to wrestle. j) When a score is indicated by two or more Judges for the same Athlete. k) When, in the opinion of the Referee, there has been a foul committed – or the situation calls for halting the bout for safety reasons. l) When requested to do so by KANSA or the Tatami Manager. m) When a Coach, or both Coaches, request a video review. n) For any other reason that the Referee deems necessary.", "page": 21}, {"article_no": "7", "section_no": "7.11", "text": "In the event that a bout starts without the time being recorded and the bout is then halted, and the remaining time is agreed upon between both coaches, the issue of the duration of the bout can no longer be protested. Rules Version 2026.01 2", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.1", "text": "A score is awarded to an Athlete when two or more judges indicate a score or when the Video Review Judge agrees on a score after a Coach has raised a Video Request.", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.2", "text": "Points are scored by a traditional karate technique with the hand or foot executed with control to the scoring area.", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.3", "text": "Only the first correctly executed technique of an exchange will score, with the exception of an effective combination of techniques, in which case the highest scoring technique will count regardless of the sequence of techniques in the combination.", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.4", "text": "The scoring areas are the body above the pelvis, up to and including the collarbone (CHUDAN), excluding the junction of the upper bone of the arm with the shoulder blades and collarbones, and the area above the collarbone (JODAN).", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.5", "text": "In order to be considered a score, the technique must have the potential to be effective if it had not been controlled, and must also fulfil the criteria of: 1) Good form (Properly executed technique). 2) Sporting attitude (Delivered without intent to cause injury). 3) Vigorous application (Delivery with speed and power). 4) Maintaining awareness of the opponent both during and after execution of the technique (Not turning away or falling down after completing a technique – unless the fall is caused by a foul by the opponent). 5) Good timing (Delivery of the technique at the correct moment). 6) Correct distance (Delivery at a distance where the technique would be effective). In order to be a valid score, a technique has to fulfil all the six scoring criteria.", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.6", "text": "The following scale is used for awarding of points: • YUKO (1 point) is awarded for TSUKI (straight punch) or UCHI (strike) to a scoring area. • WAZA ARI (2 points) is awarded for CHUDAN kicks. • IPPON (3 points) is awarded for JODAN kicks or any legal technique against an opponent whose any part of the body other than the feet is in contact with the mat, with the exception of HIZA GAMAE (One knee touching the mat while executing a technique).", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.7", "text": "Techniques to the CHUDAN area may be delivered with controlled impact without causing injury to the opponent. A loss of breath by the recipient of a blow does not in itself indicate lack of control.", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.8", "text": "Techniques to the JODAN area can score when stopped within 5 cm of the target for kicks and 2 cm for hand techniques, but may be delivered with light touch (skin touch), without causing impact, with the exception of the throat area, where no physical contact is allowed. For Cadet and U14 competitions, techniques to the JODAN area can score when stopped within 10 cm of the target for kicks and 5 cm for hand techniques, but may be delivered with light touch (skin touch), without causing impact.", "page": 22}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.9", "text": "“Skin touch” is allowed in all age categories. “Skin touch” is defined as touching the target without transferring energy into the protected helmet or head of the Athlete. Rules Version 2026.01 2", "page": 23}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.10", "text": "Correctly executed techniques landed at the moment the time runs out are valid. When using electronic judging, points must be signalled within 1.5 seconds of time expiring.", "page": 23}, {"article_no": "8", "section_no": "8.11", "text": "A technique is invalid if: a) Executed after the time-up signal or the Referee calling “YAME”. b) Executed upon or after “WAKARETE” before “TSUZUKETE” has been called. c) Executed when the performer is outside the competition area (JOGAI). d) Followed by a foul of excessive contact or otherwise causing injury. e) One turns one’s back to the opponent after a technique (lack of awareness). f) It in itself is, or follows, a violation of the rules (such as excessive contact, holding, grabbing, etc.). Rules Version 2026.01 2", "page": 24}, {"article_no": "9", "section_no": "9.1", "text": "Types of prohibited behaviour", "page": 24}, {"article_no": "9", "section_no": "9.1.1", "text": "The following behaviours are prohibited: 1) Techniques that make excessive contact, having regard to the scoring area attacked, and techniques that make contact with the throat. 2) Attacks to the arms, legs, groin, joints, or instep. 3) Attacks to the face with open-hand techniques. 4) Techniques executed after “WAKARETE” and before “TSUZUKETE” have been called. 5) Dangerous or forbidden throwing techniques. 6) Feigning or exaggerating injury. 7) Exit from the competition area (JOGAI) not caused by the opponent or following a score. 8) Self-endangerment by indulging in behaviour that exposes the Athlete to injury by the opponent, or failing to take adequate measures for self-protection (MUBOBI). 9) Avoiding combat as a means of preventing the opponent from having the opportunity to score. 10) Passivity – not attempting to engage in combat (Cannot be given in the first 15 seconds of the bout, after there are less than 15 seconds left of the bout, or to someone having a lead by points or SENSHU). 11) Clinching, wrestling, pushing, or standing chest to chest without attempting a scoring technique or takedown. 12) Grabbing the opponent with both hands for any reason other than executing a takedown upon catching the opponent’s kicking leg. 13) Grabbing the opponent’s arm or Karategi with one hand without immediately attempting a scoring technique or takedown. 14) Techniques, which by their nature, cannot be controlled for the safety of the opponent and dangerous and uncontrolled attacks. 15) Simulated or actual attacks with the head, knees, or elbows. 16) Kicking techniques against a downed opponent who is lying flat on the floor. 17) Talking to, or goading the opponent, failing to obey the orders of the Referee, discourteous behaviour towards the Refereeing officials, or other violations of etiquette.", "page": 24}, {"article_no": "9", "section_no": "9.1.2", "text": "An Athlete who delivers a scoring technique and then exits the area before the Referee calls “YAME” will be given the value of the score and JOGAI will not be imposed. If the Athlete’s attempt to score is unsuccessful, the exit will be recorded as a JOGAI.", "page": 24}, {"article_no": "9", "section_no": "9.1.3", "text": "An Athlete staying within the TATAMI can score on an opponent that is exiting, or has exited, provided that the Athlete making the score remains within the TATAMI at the moment of scoring. In such instances, the Athlete scored upon will not receive JOGAI.", "page": 24}, {"article_no": "9", "section_no": "9.1.4", "text": "A Referee may, based solely on their own Judgement, ban from the competition floor any Coach failing to conform to proper conduct, or that, in the opinion of the Referee, interferes with the orderly conduct of the bout, and postpone the continuation of a bout until the Coach complies. The same authority of the Referee extends to the compliance of other members of the Athlete’s entourage present on the competition floor. Coaches banned from the competition are not allowed to coach or guide the Athletes, in or out of the field of play. Rules Version 2026.01 2", "page": 25}, {"article_no": "9", "section_no": "9.1.5", "text": "Only the Coach designated for that specific bout is allowed to coach and guide the Athlete from the place allocated to the Coach, close to the competition area. All other registered and accredited Coaches, or other registered member of the delegation, attending the Championships are not allowed to interfere, coach and/or guide the Athlete during the same bout at the risk of having their accreditation withdrawn.", "page": 25}, {"article_no": "9", "section_no": "9.1.6", "text": "Instructions and comments from the Coach must not interfere with the proceedings. The Coach may freely speak to the Athlete when the match is halted, but must at all times refrain from commenting on judgements.", "page": 25}, {"article_no": "9", "section_no": "9.1.7", "text": "The Athlete may discreetly signal to the Coach the wish for them to request a video review. Rules Version 2026.01 2", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.1", "text": "Informal Warnings", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.1.1", "text": "Informal warnings are used to facilitate the continuity of action without stopping the bout. They are not meant to replace formal warnings when these are appropriate, and the Referee should proceed with formal warnings or penalties as appropriate if the Athletes do not react upon the informal warning.", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.1.2", "text": "There are two types of Informal Warnings: TSUZUKETE for encouraging activity To urge the Athletes to commence activity by gesturing in the same way as is customary for making the Athletes stepping on to the TATAMI, combined with the instruction “TSUZUKETE”. WAKARETE for breaking up a clinch To break-up a clinch, using the same gesture as is customary for making the Athletes step back on the TATAMI combined with giving the order “WAKARETE” to temporarily stop the action without stopping the clock. The Athletes must separate – after which the order “TSUZUKETE” is given for resuming action.", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.1.3", "text": "When WAKARETE is called when an Athlete is cornered, the Referee must ensure that the other Athlete withdraws sufficiently to disengage before TSUZUKETE is called.", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.1.4", "text": "TSUZUKTETE, unless preceded by WAKARETE, is not used if there is less than 15 seconds left of the bout.", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.1.5", "text": "An otherwise correctly executed technique will not be given a score if executed at the same time as WAKARETE has been called, but will not be penalised. An uncontrolled technique will be subject to warning or penalty in the normal manner.", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.2", "text": "Official Warnings", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.2.1", "text": "There are two degrees of official warnings - CHUI and HANSOKU CHUI: CHUI Warning is given, up to three times, for smaller infractions that do not diminish the other Athlete’s chances of winning. HANSOKU CHUI Warning of disqualification in the event of further infractions", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.3", "text": "Penalties Is given for more serious infractions that reduces the other Athlete’s chances of winning or to an Athlete for any further infraction if three CHUI has already been given.", "page": 26}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.3.1", "text": "There are two kinds of penalties, which are two different levels of disqualification: HANSOKU Disqualification from the bout. Rules Version 2026.01 2 This is the penalty of disqualification following a very serious infraction or when HANSOKU CHUI has already been given. Rules Version 2026.01 2 SHIKKAKU Disqualification from the tournament. This is a disqualification from the entire tournament including any subsequent category the offender may have been registered for. SHIKKAKU may be invoked when an Athlete fails to obey the orders of the Referee, acts maliciously, or commits an act, which harms the prestige and honour of Karate.", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.3.2", "text": "In instances where both AKA and AO are disqualified in the same bout by HANSOKU or SHIKKAKU, the opponents scheduled for the next round will win by bye (and no result is announced).", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.3.3", "text": "Serious violation of conduct, discipline, or malicious behaviour on or outside the competition area by the Athlete or their entourage may cause further disciplinary action from the WKF Disciplinary Commission or Executive Committee.", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.3.4", "text": "When a situation appears to possibly warrant a disqualification, the Referee can call one or more judges for a brief consultation (SHUGO) before announcing any decision. SHUGO is obligatory before imposing disqualifications based on time-wasting situations or in order to impose SHIKKAKU.", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4", "text": "Warning and penalty application", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.1", "text": "Excessive contact: Where contact is considered by the Referee to be too strong, but does not diminish the Athlete’s chances of winning, a warning (CHUI) may be given.", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.2", "text": "Contact causing injury: Any technique that results in injury can, unless caused by the recipient, cause a warning or penalty. The Athletes must perform all techniques with control and good form. If they cannot, then regardless of the technique misused, a warning or penalty must be imposed.", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.3", "text": "Observation after contact: The Referee must continue to observe the injured Athlete until the bout is resumed and allow adequate time for observation. A short delay in giving a judgment allows injury symptoms such as a nosebleed to develop or reveal any efforts by the Athlete to aggravate a slight injury for tactical advantage.", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.4", "text": "Overreaction to contact: A slight overreaction will receive a CHUI. An obvious display of exaggeration will receive a HANSOKU CHUI. A more serious exaggeration, such as staggering around, falling on the floor, standing up and falling down again, and so on, may receive HANSOKU directly.", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.5", "text": "Feigning an injury: Any instance of feigning an injury, however slight, will receive a minimum warning of CHUI, while an obvious display of feigning will receive a HANSOKU CHUI. A more serious display of feigning, such as feigning around, falling on the floor, standing up and falling down again, and so on, will receive SHIKKAKU directly. Any feigning of an injury from a technique that in fact has been determined by the judges as a point will, as a minimum, result in HANSOKU CHUI.", "page": 28}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.6", "text": "Contact to the throat: Any contact to the throat, unless received by the recipient’s own fault, must result in a warning or penalty. Rules Version 2026.01 2", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.7", "text": "Throwing techniques are divided into two types. The established “conventional” karate leg sweeping techniques such as De Ashi Barai, Ko Uchi Gari, etc., where the opponent is swept off-balance or thrown without being grabbed first - and those throws requiring that the opponent be grabbed by one hand or held as the throw is executed. Both are allowed.", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.8", "text": "The pivotal point of the throw must not be above the thrower’s hip level, and the opponent must be held onto throughout, so that a safe landing can be made. Over the shoulder throws are expressly forbidden, as are so-called “sacrifice” throws.", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.9", "text": "Catching a kick: The only instance where a throw may be performed while holding onto the opponent with both hands is when trapping the opponent’s kicking leg. Holding on with both hands is only permitted when grabbing an opponent’s kicking leg for the purpose of executing a takedown, and then holding on to the opponent’s leg while the other grabs the opponent’s Karategi or body to break the fall.", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.10", "text": "Grabbing the legs: It is forbidden to grab the opponent below the waist and lift and throw him/her or to reach down to pull the legs from under him/her. If an Athlete is injured as a result of a throwing technique, the Referee will decide whether a warning or penalty is called for.", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.11", "text": "One hand grabbing: The Athlete may seize the opponent’s arm or Karategi with one hand for the purpose of executing a throw or a direct scoring technique – but may not keep holding on for continuous techniques.", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.12", "text": "Holding on to break a fall: Holding on to the opponent’s Karategi with one hand is permitted to break a fall.", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.13", "text": "Exiting the competition area: JOGAI relates to a situation where an Athlete's foot, or any other part of the body, touches the floor outside of the competition area. An exception is when the Athlete is physically pushed or thrown from the area by the opponent or is exiting after having scored.", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.14", "text": "Self endangerment: A warning or penalty for MUBOBI is given when an Athlete is hit or injured through their own fault or negligence. This may be caused by turning their back on the opponent, attacking without regard for the opponent’s counterattack, stopping fighting before the Referee calls “YAME”, dropping the guard or repeated failure or refusal to block the opponent’s attacks. If an Athlete has been asked before the bout starts, and confirms wearing a groin guard, and it later proves that this is not so, the Athlete will receive SHIKKAKU. If the Athlete has not been asked, but it is discovered that the Athlete does not wear a groin guard, the Athlete will be given two (2) minutes to correct the matter and will automatically receive a warning for MUBOBI.", "page": 29}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.15", "text": "Passivity refers to situations where neither Athlete makes attempts to score, or a single Athlete does not attempt to score despite being behind on points or the opponent has a lead because of SENSHU. The Referee, before stopping the bout to give passivity, must first announce TSUZEKETE as an informal warning, using the appropriate signal and command. Passivity cannot be given during the first or last 15 seconds of a bout. Rules Version 2026.01 2", "page": 30}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.16", "text": "Avoiding Combat refers to a situation where an Athlete attempts to prevent the opponent from having the opportunity to score by using time-wasting behaviour such as constantly retreating without an effective counter, holding, clinching, or exiting the competition area rather than allowing the opponent an opportunity to score. Avoiding combat during the last 15 seconds of the bout (ATO SHIBARAKU) will, as a minimum, result in HANSOKU CHUI and loss of SENSHU.", "page": 30}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.4.17", "text": "Not following instructions: An Athlete who refuses to follow the instructions of the Referee or displays a loss of temper will automatically receive SHIKKAKU. This penalty may be imposed before, during or after the bout.", "page": 30}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.5", "text": "Excessive celebration, political or religious demonstration: Athletes are expected to respect the ceremony of salutations before and after the bout or match. Any excessive celebration, such as falling on one’s knees, etc., political or religious expressions, during or immediately after the bout or match, are prohibited and may be subject to a fine equal to the amount determined by the Executive Committee for the protest fee.", "page": 30}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.6", "text": "Disqualification of individual Athletes in Team matches", "page": 30}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.6.1", "text": "HANSOKU or SHIKKAKU: In Team matches, the offended Athlete’s score will be set at 8 points, and the offender’s score will be zeroed.", "page": 30}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.7", "text": "Disqualification in Round-robin competition.", "page": 30}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.7.1", "text": "If an Athlete receives HANSOKU, KIKEN or SHIKKAKU in a Round-robin bout, the offender’s score for the bout is set to zero while the opponent’s score is set to the higher of 4 points or points earned by techniques. Points scored by techniques retain their original value as respectively IPPON, WAZA-ARI or YUKO. Points added other than scored are all measured as YUKO.", "page": 30}, {"article_no": "10", "section_no": "10.7.2", "text": "If an Athlete receives KIKEN or SHIKKAKU in Round-robin competition, all previous bouts are voided from the result unless it is the last scheduled bout for the disqualified Athlete, in which case the result of the bout is recorded in the usual manner without consequence for the results of the previous bouts. Rules Version 2026.01 2", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.1", "text": "Athletes declared unfit to fight", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.1.1", "text": "An injured Athlete who wins a bout through disqualification due to injury is not allowed to fight again in the competition without permission from the tournament doctor. No such permission can be given to an Athlete who has suffered a loss of consciousness or otherwise has any symptoms of concussion.", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.1.2", "text": "An injured Athlete, permitted to continue, may also win a second bout by disqualification due to injury, but is immediately withdrawn from further Kumite competition in that tournament.", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.2", "text": "Procedure for handling injuries", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.2.1", "text": "When an Athlete is injured, the Referee shall at once halt the bout and call the doctor by raising his hand and verbally call out “doctor”.", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.2.2", "text": "If physically able to do so, the injured Athlete should be directed off the mat for examination and treatment by the doctor.", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.2.3", "text": "An Athlete who is injured during a bout in progress and requires medical treatment will be allowed three minutes in which to receive it. The Tatami Manager is responsible for instructing the timekeeper to start the 3-minute count. If treatment is not completed within the time allowed, the Referee will decide if the Athlete shall be declared unfit to fight, or whether an extension of treatment time shall be given.", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.2.4", "text": "10-second rule: Any Athlete who lies flat on the floor after a fall, being thrown, or knocked down, and does not fully regain their feet within ten seconds, is considered unfit to continue fighting and will be automatically withdrawn from all Kumite events in that tournament. In the event that an Athlete lies flat on the floor after a fall, being thrown, or knocked down and does not regain their feet immediately, the Referee will stop the match, call the doctor, and at the same time start a verbal count to ten in the English language, indicating his count by showing a finger for each second. In all cases where the 10 second count has been started the doctor will be asked to examine the Athlete before the bout can resume. For incidents falling under this 10-second rule, the Athlete may be examined on the mat. The Tatami Manager must notify the central table when an Athlete has been stopped from further competition based on the 10-second rule.", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.2.5", "text": "The tournament doctor is authorised to give an opinion on the injured Athlete’s fitness for continuation only. The Referee will decide the winner on the basis of HANSOKU, KIKEN, or SHIKKAKU as the case may be.", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.2.6", "text": "The Referee must be aware of pre-existing injuries when evaluating to what degree the present state of injury could be attributed to actions by the opponent. The opponent should not be penalized for any pre-existing condition.", "page": 31}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.2.7", "text": "Should an Athlete in Round-robin competition have to withdraw because of injury, all previous bouts are voided from the result unless it is the last scheduled bout for the injured Athlete, in which case the result of the bout is recorded in the usual manner without consequence for the results of the previous bouts. Rules Version 2026.01 30", "page": 32}, {"article_no": "11", "section_no": "11.3", "text": "Injury to both Athletes If two Athletes injure each other or are suffering from the effects of previously incurred injury and are declared by the Tournament Doctor to be unable to continue, the bout is decided as one normally would at full time. Rules Version 2026.01 31", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.1", "text": "General", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.1.1", "text": "When two or more Judges signal a score for the same Athlete, the Referee will stop the bout and render the decision accordingly. Should the Referee fail to stop the bout, the Match Supervisor will blow their whistle. When the Referee decides to halt the bout for any reason, they will call “YAME” at the same time using the required hand signal.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.1.2", "text": "In the event that both Athletes have a score signalled by two Judges, both Athletes will be awarded their respective points.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.1.3", "text": "If one Athlete has a score indicated by more than one Judge, and the score is different between the Judges, the higher score will be applied. The same applies if there are two judges for each Athlete with different scores.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.1.4", "text": "If there is a majority, but disagreement, among the Judges for one level of score, the majority opinion will always overrule the principle of applying the highest score.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.1.5", "text": "When explaining the basis for a decision after the bout or match, the Referee Panel may speak to the Tatami Manager, the Chief Referee, or the Appeals Jury. They will explain themselves to no one else.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2", "text": "Criteria for deciding the winner of a bout", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.1", "text": "The result of a bout is determined by an Athlete obtaining a clear lead of 8 points, at time-up having the highest number of points; at equal score, having the first unopposed point advantage (SENSHU); obtaining a decision by HANTEI or by a HANSOKU, SHIKKAKU, or KIKEN imposed against an opponent.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.2", "text": "By first unopposed score advantage (SENSHU), it is understood that one Athlete has achieved the first instance of scoring on the opponent without having the opponent also score before the signal. In instances where both Athletes score before the signal, and there is an indication of score by two judges for each of the two Athletes, no ‘first unopposed score advantage’ is awarded, and both Athletes retain the possibility of SENSHU later in the bout.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.3", "text": "In any individual bout (Individual, Round-robin, and Teams) where no superior score has been obtained by either Athlete, or the score is equal without any Athlete having a ‘first unopposed score advantage’ (SENSHU), the decision will be made based on the following criteria in order of application: a) The higher number of IPPON scored in the bout. b) The higher number of WAZA ARI scored in the bout.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.4", "text": "Should the number of IPPON and WAZA ARI be equal, the decision will be made by HANTEI, a final majority vote of the four Judges and the Referee, each casting their vote based on their individual judgement of which Athlete displayed superiority of tactics and techniques. In Round-robin and Team bouts, HIKIWAKE will be given unless it is an extra bout to decide a match outcome.", "page": 33}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.5", "text": "Individual elimination bouts cannot be declared a tie, with the exceptions of Team competition, or Round-robin competition, when a bout ends with no scores, equal scores, no Rules Version 2026.01 32 superiority in IPPON or WAZA ARI, and neither Athlete has obtained SENSHU, the Referee will announce a tie (HIKIWAKE).", "page": 34}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.6", "text": "The only time HANTEI is applied to a bout in Team competition is for an additional bout to break a tie.", "page": 34}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.7", "text": "When deciding the outcome of a bout by vote (HANTEI) at the end of an inconclusive bout, the Referee will move to the competition area perimeter and call “HANTEI”, followed by a blast of the whistle. The Judges will signal their opinions, and the Referee will declare the winner. The Referee will then indicate the winner by hand signal and the order (AKA/AO NO K ACHI), and by this action also resolve any tie.", "page": 34}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.8", "text": "Should an Athlete who has been awarded SENSHU receive a warning for avoiding combat for the following incidents: JOGAI, running away, clinching, grabbing, wrestling, pushing or standing chest to chest when there is less than 15 seconds left of the bout – the Athlete will automatically forfeit this advantage. The Referee will then first show the type of infraction and type of warning or penalty the Athlete did, then show the sign for SENSHU, followed by the sign for annulment (TORIMASEN) and at the same time announcing “AKA/AO SENSHU TORIMASEN”.", "page": 34}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.9", "text": "In cases where SENSHU has been awarded, but a successful video request determines that the other opponent also scored, and that a score in fact is not unopposed, the same procedure is used for nullification of SENSHU.", "page": 34}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.10", "text": "If SENSHU is withdrawn when it is less than 15 seconds left of the bout, no further SENSHU can be awarded to either Athlete.", "page": 34}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.2.11", "text": "In instances of Elimination competition, where both AKA and AO are disqualified in the same bout by HANSOKU, KIKEN or SHIKKAKU, the opponents scheduled for the next round will win by bye (and no result is announced), unless the double disqualification applies to a medal bout, in which case the winner will be declared based on the scores at the moment of disqualification, SENSHU, or if none of these conditions are present; by direct HANTEI. No medal can be awarded to an Athlete disqualified by SHIKKAKU.", "page": 34}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.3", "text": "Determining the winner of a round-robin group and resolving ties in individual competition", "page": 34}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.3.1", "text": "The winner of a group in Individual round robin-competition, is the Athlete having the most victory points gained by 3 points for won bouts and 1 victory Point for draws, where points are scored. In cases where there is a tie between two or more Athletes in a group, having the same number of victory Points, the criteria below will be applied in the specified order. This means that if a winner is found after one of the criteria, the following criteria will not have to be applied. 1) Winner of the bout between the Athletes involved in the tie. 2) Higher number of total scores obtained in favour through all bouts. 3) Lower number of total scores against through all bouts. 4) Higher number of IPPON obtained in favour through all bouts. 5) Lower number of IPPON against through all bouts. Rules Version 2026.01 33 6) Higher number of WAZA ARI obtained in favour through all bouts. 7) Lower number of WAZA ARI against through all bouts. 8) The highest World Ranking at the date of the competition. 9) Extra bout allowing HANTEI. For each pair compared, the criteria must be considered from the beginning of the list.", "page": 35}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.3.2", "text": "It is possible for an Athlete to be disqualified from a bout (HANSOKU) and continue the competition. In this case, their opponent wins that bout by either 4-0 (counted as YUKO) or for any score obtained exceeding 4 points.", "page": 35}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.3.3", "text": "If an already qualified Athlete is disqualified for misconduct (SHIKKAKU) at the end of the Round-robin round, the -final opponent will advance to the semi-final by bye (\"walkover\").", "page": 35}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.4", "text": "Determining the winner of a Round-robin group and resolving ties, in Team competition", "page": 35}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.4.1", "text": "The winner of a group in Team Round-robin competition is the Team having the most victory Points gained by 3 points for won matches and 1 point for draws where points are scored. In cases where there is a tie between two or more Teams in a group, having the same number of victory Points, the criteria below will be applied in the specified order. This means that if a winner is found after one of the criteria, the following criteria will not have to be applied. 1) Winner of the match between teams involved in tie. 2) Highest number of bouts won during the entire Round-robin phase. 3) Largest number of points scored during the entire Round-robin phase. 4) Least number of points scored against the Team during entire the Round-robin phase. 5) Largest number of IPPON scored by the Team during the entire Round-robin phase. 6) Least number of IPPON scored against the Team during the entire Round-robin phase. 7) Largest number of WAZA ARI scored by the Team during the entire Round-robin phase. 8) Least number of WAZA ARI scored against the Team during the entire Round-robin phase. 9) An additional bout between one of the members of each Team – if necessary, decided by HANTEI. For each pair compared, the criteria must be considered from the beginning of the list.", "page": 35}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.5", "text": "Criteria for deciding the winner of a Team match using Elimination", "page": 35}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.5.1", "text": "The winning Team is the one with the most bout victories, including those won by SENSHU. Should the two Teams have the same number of bout victories, then the winning Team will be the one with the most points.", "page": 35}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.5.2", "text": "If the two Teams have the same number of bout victories and points, then a deciding bout will be held. Each Team may nominate any one Athlete of their Team for the purpose of fighting the extra bout, regardless of whether that Athlete has already fought in a previous bout between the two Teams.", "page": 35}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.5.3", "text": "If the extra bout does not produce a winner based on superiority on points, nor any of the Athletes receive SENSHU, the extra bout will be decided based on HANTEI according to the same procedure as for individual bouts. The result of the HANTEI for the extra bout will then also determine the result of the Team match. Rules Version 2026.01 34", "page": 36}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.5.4", "text": "In Team matches, when a Team has won sufficient bout victories or scored sufficient points to be the established winner, then the match is declared over, and no further bouts will take place, except in Round-robin, where all bouts must be fought.", "page": 36}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.5.5", "text": "In Team matches, should a Team member be disqualified (HANSOKU or SHIKKAKU), their score for that bout, if any, will be zeroed, and the opponent’s score will be set at eight points.", "page": 36}, {"article_no": "12", "section_no": "12.6", "text": "Scorekeeping The Score Supervisor will use the following symbols for registration of points: 3 IPPON Three-point score 2 WAZA ARI Two-point score 1 YUKO One-point score u SENSHU First unopposed point advantage □ KACHI Winner X MAKE Loser HIKIWAKE Draw KK KIKEN Renunciation (absence) 1C CHUI (first instance) 1st warning 2C CHUI (second instance) 2nd warning 3C CHUI (third instance) 3rd warning HC HANSOKU CHUI Warning of disqualification H HANSOKU Disqualification from bout S SHIKKAKU Disqualification from tournament Rules Version 2026.01 35", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1", "text": "General provisions", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.1", "text": "No one may protest about a Judgement to the members of the Refereeing Panel.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.2", "text": "If a Refereeing procedure appears to contravene the rules, the Athlete’s Coach or their official representative are the only ones allowed to make a protest.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.3", "text": "The protest will take the form of a written report submitted immediately after the bout in which the protest was generated. The sole exception is when the protest concerns an administrative malfunction.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.4", "text": "Any protest concerning application of the rules must not necessarily impede the progression of the competition, and the intent to protest must be announced by the Coach or NF representative immediately after the end of the bout.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.5", "text": "If the protest involves Athletes in an ongoing category, then the next round that could involve the Athletes must be postponed until the appeal is decided.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.6", "text": "The Coach / NF representative will request the official protest form from the Tatami Manager. The written protest must be completed, and the protest fee submitted, within 5 minutes after receiving the protest form from the Tatami Manager.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.7", "text": "Failure of a Coach / NF representative to deliver a protest in a timely manner can lead to its rejection if such delay, in the opinion of the Appeals Jury, is without reasonable justification and impedes the progression of the competition.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.8", "text": "The Tatami Manager will complete any information regarding implicated officials and immediately hand the completed protest form to a representative of the Appeals Jury. The Appeals Jury will, without delay, review the circumstances leading to the protested decision. Having considered all the facts available, they will produce a report and shall be empowered to take such action as may be called for. The protest will be reviewed by the Appeals Jury, and as part of this review, the Jury will study the evidence available in support of the protest.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.9", "text": "The protest may also be directly decided and announced to the Appeals Jury by the RC Chairman or the Chief Referee of the event, in which case no payment of a protest fee will be applicable.", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.10", "text": "In case of an administrative malfunction during a bout in progress, the Coach can notify the Tatami Manager directly. In turn, the Tatami Manager will notify the Match Supervisor (KANSA).", "page": 37}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.11", "text": "The protest must give the name and country of the Athletes and the precise details of what is being protested. The information of officials implicated is completed by the Tatami Manager. No general claims about overall standards will be accepted as a legitimate protest. The burden of proving the validity of the protest lies with the complainant. The protest must be submitted to a representative of the Appeals Jury by the Tatami Manager. In due course, the Jury will review the circumstances leading to the protested decision. Rules Version 2026.01 36", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.12", "text": "The protester must deposit a Protest Fee as agreed by the WKF EC, and this, together with the protest, must be given to the Tatami Manager, who will turn it over to a representative of the Appeals Jury.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.13", "text": "The intent to protest must be declared as soon as the bout is finished. The written protest must be completed, and the protest fee submitted, within 5 minutes after receiving the protest form from the Tatami Manager.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.14", "text": "The decision of the Appeals Jury is final and may only be overruled by a decision of the Executive Committee upon request of the WKF President.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.1.15", "text": "The Appeals Jury may not impose sanctions or penalties. Their function is to pass judgment on the merit of the protest to start required actions from the RC and OC to take remedial action to rectify any Refereeing procedure found to contravene the rules.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.2", "text": "Composition of the Appeals Jury", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.2.1", "text": "The Appeals Jury is comprised of three Senior Referee representatives appointed by the Referee Commission (RC) or the Chief Referee. No two members may be appointed from the same National Federation. They will be numbered from 1 to 3.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.2.2", "text": "The RC will also appoint three additional members with designated numbering from 4 to 6 that automatically will replace any of the originally appointed Appeals Jury members in a conflict-of-interest situation. i.e., where the jury member is of the same nationality, has a family relationship by blood or as an In-Law with any of the parties involved or any other reasonable conflict or potential conflict of interest in the protested incident, including all members of the Refereeing panel involved in the protested incident.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.3", "text": "Appeals Evaluation Process", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.3.1", "text": "It is the responsibility of the Tatami Manager to receive the protest, to gather the Appeals Jury, and deposit the protest sum with WKF for any declined protest.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.3.2", "text": "The Appeals Jury will immediately make such inquiries and investigations as they consider necessary to validate the merit of the protest.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.3.3", "text": "Where video review is used, the Appeals Jury may request to examine the video recording of the incident before rendering a verdict.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.3.4", "text": "Each of the three members is obliged to give their verdict as to the validity of the protest. Abstentions are not acceptable.", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.4", "text": "Declined and accepted protests", "page": 38}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.4.1", "text": "If a protest is found invalid, the Appeals Jury will appoint one of its members to verbally notify the protester that the protest has been declined, mark the original document with the word “DECLINED”, have it signed by each of the members of the Appeals Jury, and inform the protester of the decision. Rules Version 2026.01 37", "page": 39}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.4.2", "text": "If a protest is accepted, the appeals Jury will liaise with the Organising Commission (OC) and the Chief Referee to take such measures as can be practically carried out to remedy the situation, including the possibilities of: • Reversing previous judgments that contravene the rules. • Voiding results of the affected rounds from the point before the incident. • Redoing such bouts that have been affected by the incident. • Issuing a recommendation to the RC for any involved Judges evaluated for sanction.", "page": 39}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.4.3", "text": "The responsibility rests with the Appeals Jury to exercise restraint and sound judgment in taking actions that will disturb the program of the event in any significant manner. Reversing the process of the Eliminations is a last option to secure a fair outcome.", "page": 39}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.4.4", "text": "If the protest is accepted, the Appeals Jury will appoint one of its members who will verbally notify the protester that the protest has been accepted, mark the original document with the word “ACCEPTED”, and have it signed by each of the members of the Appeals Jury, before depositing the protest with the Chief Referee, and returning the protest fee to the protester.", "page": 39}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.4.5", "text": "An accepted protest does not mean that a bout or match will automatically be redone.", "page": 39}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.5", "text": "Incident report", "page": 39}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.5.1", "text": "After handling the incident in the above prescribed manner, the Appeals Jury will meet again and elaborate a simple protest incident report, describing their findings and stating their reason(s) for accepting or rejecting the protest.", "page": 39}, {"article_no": "13", "section_no": "13.5.2", "text": "The report should be signed by all three members of the Appeals Jury and submitted to the Chief Referee and the Organising Commission. Rules Version 2026.01 38", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.1", "text": "In WKF World Championships, Premier League, Olympic Games, Youth Olympic Games, Continental Games, World Games, and multisport games of this nature, the use of video review of bouts is required. Use of video review is also recommended for other competitions whenever possible.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.2", "text": "The video review is initiated when a Coach raises their video review card (manually or by electronic device as applicable) to signal that a possible score of their Athlete that was missed by the judges. If a Coach pushes the joy stick’s button and then immediately regrets it, the procedure will not be stopped, and the video review will take place accordingly. The Coach should stand up during the video review to make the Referee aware and avoid continuation of the bout if the system malfunctions.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.3", "text": "In competitions where Coaches are provided electronic equipment that allows requesting review for specifically YUKO, WAZA ARI or IPPON, the Video Review Judge is only required to evaluate a possible score for the type of point requested. The Coach may change the level of the score up until the Referee finishes the signal for video review.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.4", "text": "If the Athlete wishes to have the Coach request a video review or refrain from raising a review, this must be discreetly signalled without disturbing the progress of the bout.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.5", "text": "The video review can be requested by the Coach in instances where the Judges awarded a lower score than, in the opinion of the Coach, should be for a higher scoring technique.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.6", "text": "The Video Review Judge may only award points if the Athlete for whom the request was raised had a valid score, i.e. scoring before or simultaneously with the other Athlete.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.7", "text": "An exception from above sub article is when neither Athlete has been awarded a point by the corner Judges, only one of the Coaches calls a Video review, the other Coach has no card or do not wish a video request – in which case only the techniques of the Athlete whom video review is called for will be considered for scoring.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.8", "text": "The last 6 seconds before the bout was stopped for the request will always be evaluated, but additional time can be added as deemed necessary to make the best possible decision. The sequence must be reviewed at normal speed but can in addition be viewed in slow motion or zoom if necessary. The review must always first be done at full speed, although slow motion may subsequently be used to determine details. The total time used for reviewing the video is not to exceed 30 seconds, after which a decision must be rendered.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.09", "text": "If both Coaches request video review at the same time, the Video Review Judge may only award the point to whoever is deemed to score first. The only exception being simultaneous scoring techniques, in which case points can be awarded to both Athletes.", "page": 40}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.10", "text": "If one Coach shows the card for video review and the other Coach wants a review of the same instance, the second Coach must raise his card before the review starts in order not to lose his right to request video review for that instance. The video review is considered started when the Referee makes the gesture. Rules Version 2026.01 39", "page": 41}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.11", "text": "If the request is found valid, a red or blue card, with the number 3 for IPPON, 2 for WAZA ARI or 1 for YUKO is raised or the outcome displayed on the monitor. The Referee will then award the score in the usual manner. If the request is found invalid, the Coach will lose the right to raise another video request for the remainder of the bout.", "page": 41}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.12", "text": "The Video Review Judge may not overrule any decision by the corner judges with the exception of SENSHU.", "page": 41}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.13", "text": "If the Video Review Judge is unable to observe the technique(s) due to camera angle, they will signal this by doing the gesture for MIENAI, and the Coach will retain the card. In the case of technical problems (electricity, camera, or computer malfunctions etc.) it is not possible to analyse the video and make a decision, the same procedure will apply, and the Coach will retain the card.", "page": 41}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.15", "text": "If a Coach requests VR, but in the opinion of the Referee the technique was uncontrolled or too hard, a warning or penalty must be applied, and the Coach will retain the card.", "page": 41}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.16", "text": "Once WAKARETE is called by the Referee, the Coaches do not have the opportunity to make a video request, unless the technique happened before WAKARETE was called.", "page": 41}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.17", "text": "It remains the duty of the Coach to protest if a VR card is not returned whenever the Coach has the right to have the card returned by the Tatami Manager.", "page": 41}, {"article_no": "14", "section_no": "14.18", "text": "The following table determines the video review cards allowable per phase for WKF events: Rules Version 2026.01 40", "page": 42}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.1", "text": "Chief Referee and the Referee Commission", "page": 42}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.1.1", "text": "The Chief Referee and the Referee Commission’s powers and duties shall be as follows: 1) To ensure the correct preparation for each given tournament in consultation with the Organising Commission, with regard to competition area arrangement, the provision and deployment of all equipment and necessary facilities, bout/match operation and supervision, safety precautions, etc. 2) To appoint and deploy the Tatami Managers and Tatami Manager Assistants to their respective areas and to act upon and take such action as may be required by the reports of the Tatami Managers. 3) To supervise and coordinate the overall performance of the refereeing officials. 4) To nominate substitute officials where such are required. 5) To pass the final Judgement on matters of a technical nature which may arise during a given bout or match and for which there are no stipulations in the rules. 6) To appoint the Appeals Jury for the competition.", "page": 42}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.2", "text": "Tatami Managers and Tatami Manager Assistants", "page": 42}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.2.1", "text": "The Tatami Manager’s powers and duties shall be as follows: 1) To delegate, appoint, and supervise the Referees and Judges for all bouts and matches in areas under their control. 2) To oversee the performance of the Referees and Judges in their areas, and to ensure that the Officials appointed are capable of the tasks allotted to them. 3) To supervise that KANSA stops the bout to instruct the Referee regarding a contravention of the Rules of Competition. 4) To prepare a daily, written report on the performance of each official under their supervision, together with their recommendations, if any, to the Referee Commission. 5) To appoint one Referee with WKF Referee A Qualification to act as Video Review Judge. (VRJ).", "page": 42}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.3", "text": "Referees", "page": 42}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.3.1", "text": "The Referee’s powers shall be as follows: 1) The Referee (“SHUSHIN”) shall have the power to conduct bouts/matches, including announcing the start, the suspension, and the end of the bout or match. 2) The Referee shall give all commands and make all announcements. 3) To award points based on the decision of the Judges. 4) To stop the bout when an injury, illness or inability of an Athlete to continue is noticed. 5) To stop the bout when, in the Referee’s opinion, a foul has been committed, or to ensure the safety of the Athletes. 6) To call FUKUSHIN SHUGO (summoning the judges) for giving SHIKKAKU and disqualification for wasting time - or when in the opinion of the Referee it is deemed necessary to call FUKUSHIN SHUGO for; applying the 10-second rule; when the doctor wants to withdraw an Athlete; or when directly giving HANSOKU. 7) To indicate fouls observed and impose warnings and penalties as required by the rules. 8) To explain to the Tatami Manager, Referee Commission, or Appeals Jury, if necessary, the basis for giving a Judgement. 9) To announce and start an extra bout when required in Team matches. Rules Version 2026.01 41 10) To conduct voting of the Judges, in the event of a tied bout, and if necessary, including their own vote (HANTEI) to break a tie. 11) To announce the winner. 12) The authority of the Referee is not confined solely to the competition area but also to its entire immediate perimeter, including controlling the conduct of Coaches, other Athletes, or any part of the Athletes’ entourage, present on the competition floor.", "page": 43}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.4", "text": "Judges", "page": 43}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.4.1", "text": "The Judges (FUKUSHIN) powers shall be as follows: 1) To signal points scored on their own initiative. 2) To exercise their right to vote on any decision to be taken. 3) To advise the Referee on possible disqualifications if called by FUKUSHIN SHUGO.", "page": 43}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.4.2", "text": "The Judges shall carefully observe the actions of the Athletes and signal to the Referee an opinion when a score is observed.", "page": 43}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.5", "text": "Match Supervisors (KANSA)", "page": 43}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.5.1", "text": "The Match Supervisor (KANSA) will assist the Tatami Manager by overseeing the match or bout in progress. Should decisions of the Referee and/or Judges not be in accordance with the Rules of Competition, the Match Supervisor will immediately signal by blowing their whistle.", "page": 43}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.5.2", "text": "Records kept of the match shall become official records subject to the approval of the Match Supervisor.", "page": 43}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.5.3", "text": "Before the start of each match or bout, Kansa Assistants will ensure that Athletes’ equipment and Karategi are in accordance with the WKF rules of competition. In competitions where Kansa Assistant is not applicable or available, it is the responsibility of the KANSA to ensure that the equipment is in accordance with the rules before each bout.", "page": 43}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.5.4", "text": "In the following situations, the Match Supervisor (KANSA) will signal by blowing their whistle: 1) The Referee forgets to indicate SENSHU. 2) The Referee forgets to remove the SENSHU. 3) The Referee gives a score to the wrong Athlete. 4) The Referee gives a warning/penalty to the wrong Athlete. 5) The Referee gives a score to an Athlete and a warning for exaggeration to the other. 6) The Referee gives a score to an Athlete and MUBOBI to the other. 7) The Referee gives a score for a technique done after YAME or after the time is up. 8) The Referee gives a score made by an Athlete when the Athlete is outside the fighting area. 9) The Referee gives a warning or penalty for passivity during ATO SHIBARAKU. 10) The Referee gives the wrong warning or penalty during ATO SHIBARAKU. 11) The Referee gives a direct HANSOKU CHUI during ATO SHIBARAKU, but the incident happened just before ATO SHIBARAKU signal. 12) The Referee doesn’t stop the bout, and there are two or more judges signalling a point scored. 13) The Referee doesn’t stop the bout when a Video Review is requested by a Coach. 14) The Referee doesn’t follow the majority of scores signalled by the judges. 15) The Referee doesn’t call the doctor in a 10-second rule situation. 16) The Referee does HANTEI/HIKIWAKE, but SENSHU has been obtained. Rules Version 2026.01 42 17) A Judge(s) is holding the flags or electronic device in the wrong hand. 18) The scoreboard is not showing the correct information. 19) The technique requested by the Coach was done after YAME or after the time was up. 20) The Referee did not observe a JOGAI. 21) For any other unforeseen situation that reasonably requires the bout to be halted. 22) In instances where KANSA is in doubt about a verdict, KANSA has the right to check the video review recording.", "page": 44}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.5.5", "text": "In the following situations, the Match Supervisor will not get involved with the Referee Panel’s decision: 1) The Judges don’t signal for a score. 2) KANSA has no vote or authority in matters of judgments, such as whether a score was valid or not, unless there has been an error in the application of the rules.", "page": 44}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.6", "text": "Score Supervisors", "page": 44}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.6.1", "text": "The Score Supervisor will keep a separate record of the scores and warnings awarded by the Referee and, at the same time, oversee the actions of the appointed score/time-keeper.", "page": 44}, {"article_no": "15", "section_no": "15.6.2", "text": "In the event that the Referee does not hear the time-up bell, the Score-Supervisor will blow his whistle, not KANSA. Rules Version 2026.01 43", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.1", "text": "Age", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.1.1", "text": "Allocation of age category is determined by the age of the Athlete on the first day of competition of the event.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.1.2", "text": "In the senior Kumite categories, Athletes must be 18 years old.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.1.3", "text": "Participants in Under 21 categories must be 18, 19 or 20 years old, Junior categories must be 16 or 17 years old, Cadet categories must be 14 or 15 years old, and Under 14 categories must be 12 or 13 years old.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.2", "text": "NF Quota per Event", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.2.1", "text": "Each National Federation at the Cadet, Junior, & U21 World Championships, Individual World Senior Championships - ¨Final Phase¨, and the Team World Senior Championships is limited to 1 Athlete per category.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.2.2", "text": "Specific limitations may apply at the Individual Senior World Championships - ¨Qualification Phase. ¨ If an NF already has a qualified athlete in a category of the Individual Senior World Championships - ¨Final Phase¨, they may not register another athlete for the same category in the Individual World Championships - ¨Qualification Phase.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.2.3", "text": "Karate 1 -Events are open competitions where all WKF members are permitted to participate without restriction of 1 Athlete per NF. Notwithstanding, participants must be members of a National Federation that is recognized by the WKF.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.2.4", "text": "Multi-sport Events like the ANOC- Beach Games, World Games, and Olympics may apply other criteria, to be defined in their respective Qualification System.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3", "text": "Nationality", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.1", "text": "With the following exceptions, only Nationals of a country may take part in the World Championships and WKF official events representing their country.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.2", "text": "As a general rule, an Athlete who has represented one country in a WKF official event or World Championships cannot represent another country at an official WKF event or a World Championships.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.3", "text": "Nevertheless, if an Athlete who has taken part in one of those events obtains by marriage the nationality of the spouse, they may represent the spouse’s country.", "page": 45}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.4", "text": "An Athlete who possesses dual nationality (i.e. one by virtue of the law of one country, the other by virtue of the law of another country) may only represent one or another country as the Athlete in question selects. Once having represented both countries, WKF EC approval will be necessary for a further change, following a reasoned written demand by the relevant NF to the WKF President. Rules Version 2026.01 44", "page": 46}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.5", "text": "An Athlete may represent the country of their birth and of which the Athlete is a National unless they opt to take the nationality of their father or mother.", "page": 46}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.6", "text": "A naturalized Athlete (or one who has changed their nationality by naturalization) may not participate in the World Championships representing their new country until three years after their naturalization. The period following naturalization may be reduced or even cancelled with the agreement of the two NFs concerned and the final approval of the WKF EC.", "page": 46}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.7", "text": "If an associated State, Province or Overseas Department, a Country or former Colony acquires independence, or a country incorporated within another country by reason of a change of border, or if a new NF is recognized by WKF, an Athlete may continue to represent the country to which they belong or belonged. However, they may choose to represent their new country or their new NF in the World Championships.", "page": 46}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.8", "text": "In instances where the WKF has recognized more than 1 (one) NF for which members hold the same national passport (i.e., for a country and its protectorates with separate governing national sporting bodies), the Athlete may only compete for the NF of residence, provided that has not yet competed for the other (s) NF(s) in WKF official events.", "page": 46}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.9", "text": "In order to get the transfer to another NF of which the nationals hold the same passport, it will be enough with the agreement between the 2 (two) NFs involved to confirm any change to the WKF concerning the status of an Athlete. In case of disagreement between the NFs, any change will have to be approved by the WKF EC. In this case, the Athlete, through the NF concerned, will have to prove to the WKF’s satisfaction the residency in the territory governed by the other NF, or failing this, the relationship with the other NF that makes the change justifiable.", "page": 46}, {"article_no": "16", "section_no": "16.3.10", "text": "Once the Athlete has represented all the NFs involved, the WKF EC approval will be necessary for any further change. Rules Version 2026.01 45", "page": 47}, {"article_no": "17", "section_no": "17.1", "text": "National Federations may modify these rules for the purpose of national competitions or other competitions not on the official WKF programme, as long as no alterations are made to rules pertaining to the safety of the Athletes, use of protective equipment, scoring, prohibited behaviour, warning and penalties, injuries and accidents in competition, or criteria for decision.", "page": 47}, {"article_no": "17", "section_no": "17.2", "text": "National Federations are encouraged to consult their national sports authorities for guidance on national law and/or guidelines for competitive sports for children under 12 years of age.", "page": 47}, {"article_no": "17", "section_no": "17.3", "text": "Any deviation from the Competition Rules applied to a competition must be announced in the official bulletin or invitation to the event. Rules Version 2026.01 46", "page": 48}, {"article_no": "18", "section_no": "18.1", "text": "From time to time, situations may occur where the rules fall short of giving specific instructions to resolve an issue. In such instances, the Chief Referee for the competition has the authority to resolve the issue by applying analogous resolutions to similar cases found in the rules or their best judgment. Before making a decision, the Chief Referee may consult the assigned WKF Representative for the tournament or escalate the issue to the Sports Commissioner for consultation before taking a decision.", "page": 48}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "SHOBU HAJIME", "text": "Start the Match or Bout — After the announcement, the Referee takes a step back.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "ATO SHIBARAKU", "text": "A little more time left — An audible signal will be given by the timekeeper 15 seconds before the actual end of the bout and the Referee will announce “Ato Shibaraku”.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "YAME", "text": "Stop — Interruption, or end of the bout. As they make the announcement, the Referee makes a downward chopping motion with his hand.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "MOTO NO ICHI", "text": "Original position — Athletes and Referee return to their starting positions.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "TSUZUKETE", "text": "Fight on — Resumption of fighting ordered after WAKARETE, when an unauthorised interruption occurs, or when the Referee gives an informal order to commence fighting due to lack of activity.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "TSUZUKETE HAJIME", "text": "Resume fighting, Begin — The Referee stands in a forward stance. As they say “Tsuzukete” they extend their arms, palms outwards towards the Athletes. As they say “Hajime” they turn the palms and bring them rapidly towards one another, at the same time stepping back.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "FUKUSHIN SHUGO", "text": "Judges called — The Referee calls the Judges to assemble.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "HANTEI", "text": "Decision — Referee calls for a decision at the end of an inconclusive bout. After a two-tone short blast of the whistle, the Judges signal their votes, and the Referee indicates the winner by raising their arm.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "HIKIWAKE", "text": "Draw — In case of a tied bout, the Referee crosses his arms, then extends them with the palms showing to the front.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "AKA (AO) NO KACHI", "text": "Red (Blue) wins — The Referee raises their arm on the side of the winner.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "AKA (AO) IPPON", "text": "Red (Blue) scores three points — The Referee raises their arm up at 45 degrees on the side of the scorer.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "AKA (AO) WAZA-ARI", "text": "Red (Blue) scores two points — The Referee extends their arm at shoulder level on the side of the scorer.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "AKA (AO) YUKO", "text": "Red (Blue) scores one point — The Referee extends their arm downward at 45 degrees on the side of the scorer.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "CHUI", "text": "Warning — The Referee shows the signal for the type of offense towards the offender followed by showing 1 to 3 fingers depending on if this is the 1st, 2nd or 3rd warning.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "HANSOKU-CHUI", "text": "Warning of disqualification — The Referee shows the signal for the type of offense towards the offender followed by pointing with one finger towards the offender's belt.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "HANSOKU", "text": "Disqualification — The Referee points to the face of the offender and announces a win for the opponent.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "JOGAI", "text": "Exit from the competition area not caused by the opponent — The Referee points their index finger to the side of the offender to indicate that the Athlete has moved out of the area followed by the applicable warning or penalty.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "SENSHU", "text": "First unopposed point advantage — After awarding the point in the regular fashion, the Referee calls “AKA (AO) SENSHU” while lifting their bent arm with the palm facing the Referee's own face.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "SHIKKAKU", "text": "Disqualification from the tournament — The Referee points to the face of the offender, then away from the competition area, and announces a win for the opponent.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "TORIMASEN", "text": "Cancellation — A decision is annulled. The Referee crosses their hands in a downward movement.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "KIKEN", "text": "Renunciation — The Referee points downwards at 45 degrees in the direction of the Athlete's or Team's side of the Tatami.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "MUBOBI", "text": "Self-Endangerment — The Referee touches their face then, turning their hand edge forward, moves it back and forth to indicate that the Athlete endangered himself.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App1", "section_no": "WAKARETE", "text": "“Separate” — The Referee motions for the Athletes to separate from a clinch, or standing chest to chest, by separating his hands with a motion with the palms outward while giving the verbal order. The Athletes halt action and separate until receiving the order “Tsuzukete”.", "page": 49}, {"article_no": "App2", "section_no": "Starting and stopping the bout", "text": "Illustrated gestures for: SHOMEN NI REI; OTAGAI NI REI; SHOBU HAJIME; MOTO NO ICHI; YAME. (Photographic plates in the source document — captions only, no accompanying prose.)", "page": 50}, {"article_no": "App2", "section_no": "Points and cancellations", "text": "Illustrated gestures for: YUKO; WAZA ARI; IPPON; SENSHU; TORIMASEN (cancellation). (Photographic plates in the source document — captions only, no accompanying prose.)", "page": 50}, {"article_no": "App2", "section_no": "Warnings", "text": "Illustrated gestures for: TSUZUKETE; WAKARETE; PASSIVITY; HARD CONTACT OR DANGEROUS THROWS; EXAGGERATING INJURY; FEIGNING INJURY; JOGAI. (Photographic plates in the source document — captions only, no accompanying prose.)", "page": 50}, {"article_no": "App2", "section_no": "Warnings (continued)", "text": "Illustrated gestures for: MUBOBI; AVOIDING COMBAT; PUSHING; GRABBING; UNCONTROLLED ATTACK; SIMULATED ATTACK (ELBOW / HEAD / KNEE); GOADING OR TALKING; CHUI #1, #2, #3; HANSOKU CHUI. (Photographic plates in the source document — captions only, no accompanying prose.)", "page": 50}, {"article_no": "App2", "section_no": "Decision", "text": "Illustrated gestures for: FUKUSHIN SHUGO; AKA (AO) KIKEN; HANTEI; HANSOKU; SHIKKAKU; HIKIWAKE; AKA (AO) NO KACHI. (Photographic plates in the source document — captions only, no accompanying prose.)", "page": 50}, {"article_no": "App2", "section_no": "Video review signals", "text": "Illustrated gestures for: VIDEO REVIEW; MIENAI. (Photographic plates in the source document — captions only, no accompanying prose.)", "page": 50}, {"article_no": "App2", "section_no": "Flag signals (sitting position)", "text": "Illustrated gestures for: YUKO; WAZA ARI; IPPON. (Photographic plates in the source document — captions only, no accompanying prose.)", "page": 50}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Male Senior (18+)", "text": "Weight categories: 60, 67, 75, 84, +84 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Female Senior (18+)", "text": "Weight categories: 50, 55, 61, 68, +68 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Male U21 (18 to <21)", "text": "Weight categories: 60, 67, 75, 84, +84 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Female U21 (18 to <21)", "text": "Weight categories: 50, 55, 61, 68, +68 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Male Junior (16 to <18)", "text": "Weight categories: 55, 61, 68, 76, +76 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Female Junior (16 to <18)", "text": "Weight categories: 48, 53, 59, 66, +66 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Male Cadet (14 to <16)", "text": "Weight categories: 52, 57, 63, 70, +70 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Female Cadet (14 to <16)", "text": "Weight categories: 47, 54, 61, +61 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Male U14 (12 to <14)", "text": "Weight categories: 40, 45, 50, 55, +55 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App3", "section_no": "Female U14 (12 to <14)", "text": "Weight categories: 42, 47, 52, +52 kg.", "page": 55}, {"article_no": "App4", "section_no": "Form fields", "text": "A prepaid WKF Official Protest Form recording: date, competition, place, category; AKA and AO competitors' countries; name/country/signature of the Coach or NF representative (valid as receipt by the WKF); Tatami number and KANSA; the full Referee Panel (Referee, Judges 1-4, responsible Tatami Manager, Score Supervisor, VR Judge) with name and country; and a free-text protest description.", "page": 56}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "1", "text": "When using the two-corner judge system, the corner Judges and the Referee all have mutual responsibility for points. Flags are used by the Corner Judges for signalling.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "2", "text": "In addition to showing points, the Corner Judges will assist the Referee by giving signals for JOGAI and excessive contact, but the Referee remains autonomous in applying warnings and penalties, and will only be overruled by two judges indicating the same foul.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "3", "text": "Points are awarded if two Judges, or one Judge plus the Referee, agree on the score.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "4", "text": "In order to be able to cover all three angles of view, the referee should never position themselves on the same side as the two Judges.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "5", "text": "The Coaches should be placed in front of the Referee and not behind.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "6", "text": "The Referee can show and ask for support for points that are made in their field of play. In this case, the Referee's signals for YUKO, WAZA ARI and IPPON are the same as in the regular Kumite rules, with the exception that the Referee's elbow is touching their torso while indicating the respective signal. After the Referee has received support, the signals when giving points are the same as for bouts under regular rules.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "7", "text": "If one Judge signals for a point and the other for a warning or penalty, the Referee will take the final decision by supporting one of the Judges.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "8", "text": "If the two Judges, or one Judge and the Referee, show different points for the same Athletes, the higher will be given.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "9", "text": "If one judge indicates a score but the Referee disagrees, the Referee will show the gesture for TORIMASEN without stopping the bout.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "10", "text": "If both Judges signal a point, but for different Athletes, the Referee may award both points.", "page": 57}, {"article_no": "App5", "section_no": "Additional flag signals", "text": "Two extra flag signals unique to this system: JOGAI (tapping the floor to the side) and CONTACT (crossing the flags to the side of the face).", "page": 58}, {"article_no": "App6", "section_no": "Summary table", "text": "A one-page tabular summary (image, not extractable as text) of the winning criteria and tie-resolution ladder already set out in prose in Article 12 — see Art. 12.2.1 (criteria for deciding a bout), Art. 12.2.3 (equal-score tiebreak order), Art. 12.3.1 (individual Round-robin group ties), and Art. 12.4.1 (Team Round-robin group ties).", "page": 59}];
